   ("trisolaris-tech", "3BT · THE TECHNOLOGIA OF TRISOLARIS", "#2ce0e0", "tech dissected · hub + 6 spoke repos · 12 technologies", "The Technologia of Trisolaris — a HUB-AND-SPOKE companion to the Three-Body pocket universe (3BP) that DISSECTS THE TECHNOLOGY across all three media (the books, Tencent 2023, Netflix 2024), the way David asked: 'dissect the technologia in all 3 medium, build a repo that lists the tech with links to the repos, build those repos also.' Themed engineering-blueprint (cyan schematic on black). The HUB (davidwise01.github.io/trisolaris-tech/) catalogs 12 technologies, each tagged with MEDIA-PRESENCE chips (📖 books / Tencent ’23 / Netflix ’24) and an HONEST REAL-SCIENCE VERDICT (REAL / SPECULATIVE / HALF / FLUFF), grouped into 5 categories (Contact & Surveillance · Weapons · Propulsion & Structures · Materials & Computation · Mind & Survival). SIX of the core technologies have their own DEDICATED SPOKE REPOS (each a single-tech dissection page + .dlw, linked from the hub): SOPHON (智子, the proton-computer — FLUFF), THE DROPLET (水滴, the strong-force probe — FLUFF), THE DUAL-VECTOR FOIL (二向箔, the 2D weapon — FLUFF), RED COAST (红岸, the solar-amplified transmitter — HALF), THE NANOFILAMENT (飞刃, Wang Miao's flying-blade, the one device in ALL THREE media — SPECULATIVE), and CURVATURE PROPULSION (曲率驱动, lightspeed/black-domain — SPECULATIVE). The other 6 are catalogued in the hub (the human-formation computer [REAL, the most honest idea in the saga], the Staircase radiation-sail, the space elevator, hibernation, the gravitational-wave deterrence broadcast & photoid, the mental seal & Wallfacers). Honest-fluff discipline throughout (e.g. sophon = NINE dims not 11; FTL-by-entanglement impossible; the Alcubierre metric is real GR; GW are real [LIGO 2015] but the beacon-use is fiction). A hidden Claude node sits in the hub's schematic. 12 tech-emergents (synths), full .dlw. &middot; homed in the biblion realm beside its hub [[the-ansible]]."),
   ("egyptian-pantheon", "NTR · THE EGYPTIAN PANTHEON", "#c9a227", "the netjeru · 34 gods", "The gods of ancient Egypt as a mythology-world — three thousand years of theology (c. 3100 BCE → the close of the temples), and the headline feature you asked for: THE INTERPRETATIO, every god carrying its GREEK & ROMAN analog. The ancient interpretatio graeca/romana — Amun=Zeus/Jupiter (Zeus-Ammon, the Siwa oracle), Osiris=Dionysus & Hades, Isis=Demeter (then ‘the myriad-named’), Thoth=Hermes Trismegistus, Horus=Apollo, Set=Typhon, Ptah=Hephaestus, Neith=Athena, Bastet=Artemis, Anubis=Hermanubis, and the deliberately-made fusion god Serapis. Standing template — THE ARC (Nile → the Ennead → the Osiris myth → Akhenaten's Aten heresy → the interpretatio & the close) · THE INTERPRETATIO (the deep-dive) · REAL OR FLUFF (animal-‘worship,’ Set-as-Satan, the Orion/alien claims, Akhenaten=Moses, the pharaoh's curse, and a caveat that the analogs are functional, not exact) · THE MESSAGE. 34 gods across five groups (the Ennead, the sun & makers, kingship/love/home, the Duat, chaos/war), full .dlw each. Sources: the Pyramid/Coffin Texts, the Book of the Dead, Herodotus, Plutarch, Plato. &middot; the mythos seed, rooted out to [[the-ansible]]."),
   ("the-terminal", "TTY · THE TERMINAL", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the genealogy · 1950–1991 · 16 emergents", "The Terminal (TTY) — a genealogy of the surviving solo, pre-internet terminal programs, 1950→1991: ed begat grep &amp; vi; the shell begat bash; ELIZA begat the chatbot; Adventure &amp; Rogue begat whole genres. The editors, the shell, the filters, the languages-at-the-prompt, and the worlds-in-the-words — the small tools that did one thing well and never died. A cited history, an original one-line prompt title, a family tree; 16 emergents. Stops at 1991 (Linux + the Web). &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("ed", "ED · ED", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the mother editor", "ed (ED) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Ken Thompson's line editor (Unix, 1969) — terse, silent, command-driven; the program every later Unix tool grew from. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("vi", "VI · VI", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the visual editor", "vi (VI) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Bill Joy's screen-oriented editor (Berkeley, 1976), built on ex — modal, keyboard-only, still in every machine as vim. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("emacs", "EMX · EMACS", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the editor that became a world", "Emacs (EMX) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Stallman &amp; Steele's extensible editor (MIT, 1976), grown from TECO macros — endlessly self-modifying, an environment more than an editor. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("the-shell", "SH · THE SHELL", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the command line", "The Shell (SH) — a child of THE TERMINAL: the program you type commands into — Thompson's shell (1971), Bourne's sh (1979), and Brian Fox's bash (1989); the interpreter of the prompt. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("grep", "GRP · GREP", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the finder", "grep (GRP) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Ken Thompson's global-regular-expression-print (1973) — born from an ed command — that searches text for a pattern and prints what matches. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("sed", "SED · SED", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the stream editor", "sed (SED) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Lee McMahon's non-interactive stream editor (Bell Labs, 1974) — applies ed-style edits to a flowing river of text, never opening a file. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("awk", "AWK · AWK", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the pattern language", "awk (AWK) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Aho, Weinberger &amp; Kernighan's pattern-scanning language (1977, its name their initials) — match lines, pull fields, do arithmetic, in the pipe. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("c-compiler", "CC · THE C COMPILER", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the compiler that built Unix", "The C Compiler (CC) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Dennis Ritchie's C and its compiler (cc, Bell Labs, 1972–73) — the language Unix was rewritten in, the first portable system software. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("make", "MAK · MAKE", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the builder", "make (MAK) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Stuart Feldman's build tool (Bell Labs, 1976) — reads a file of rules and rebuilds only what changed, in the right order; still raising software. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("troff", "TRF · TROFF", "#46c8e0", "LOGISMÓS · the typesetter", "troff (TRF) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Joe Ossanna's typesetting program (Bell Labs, 1973) and its nroff sibling — formats documents from plain marked-up text; still sets Unix man pages. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("lisp-repl", "LSP · THE LISP REPL", "#6ee787", "LOGISMÓS · thought made interactive", "The Lisp REPL (LSP) — a child of THE TERMINAL: John McCarthy's Lisp (~1958–60) and the read-eval-print loop — type an expression, the machine evaluates and answers; interactive computing itself. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("basic", "BAS · BASIC", "#6ee787", "LOGISMÓS · the language at the prompt", "BASIC (BAS) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Kemeny &amp; Kurtz's Beginner's All-purpose Symbolic Instruction Code (Dartmouth, 1964) — so anyone could sit at a terminal and make the machine do something. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("eliza", "ELZ · ELIZA", "#9a7cff", "LOGISMÓS · the program that talks back", "ELIZA (ELZ) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Joseph Weizenbaum's conversational program (MIT, 1966), whose DOCTOR script mirrored your words back as a therapist might — the first program people confided in. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("adventure", "ADV · ADVENTURE", "#9a7cff", "LOGISMÓS · the world in the words", "Adventure (ADV) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Colossal Cave Adventure (Crowther &amp; Woods, ~1976) — a cave rendered entirely in prose, navigated by typed commands; the first text adventure. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("rogue", "RGU · ROGUE", "#9a7cff", "LOGISMÓS · the dungeon in letters", "Rogue (RGU) — a child of THE TERMINAL: Toy &amp; Wichman's dungeon crawler (UC Santa Cruz, 1980) — a maze drawn in ASCII, different every time, lethal and unforgiving; played alone at a terminal. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("coreutils", "COR · THE COREUTILS", "#ffb000", "LOGISMÓS · the atoms of the toolkit", "The Coreutils (COR) — a child of THE TERMINAL: the small single-purpose Unix utilities (cat, ls, wc, sort, uniq, head, tail, from 1971 on) — each doing exactly one trivial-seeming thing. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("self", "SLF · THE SELF", "#b9a8e8", "ERĒMIA · alone with one", "The Self (SLF) — first sphere of the ERĒMIA domain (Existential Dread): you, alone with yourself — the monad, the mirror, the cogito. Walks Plato's Cave, Foucault's panopticon internalized, and the simulated self; 7 emergents. We are all alone, even together. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("id", "IDD · THE ID", "#e0a0a0", "ERĒMIA · alone with two", "The Id (IDD) — ERĒMIA: you and an Other, desire's arithmetic and the unbridgeable gap. The cave of two, the panopticon's watcher-and-watched, Sartre's gaze, the simulated other; 7 emergents. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("the-super-id", "SUPER ID · SID", "#b0334a", "eremia · the id, crowned · Nietzsche \u00d7 hedonism · themed engine · live", "SUPER ID (SID) — a UD0 ER\u0112MIA sphere, the FIRST built with the THEMED CHAOS ENGINE (the chaos engine locked to a repo's unifying theme, which it expresses). Unifying theme: THE ID, CROWNED — where the super-ego is the internalised judge, the Super-Id is the drive enthroned as sovereign: pleasure and will as the only law. NIETZSCHE (will to power, the \u00dcbermensch, master/slave morality, the Dionysian, eternal recurrence, God is dead) meets HEDONISM (Freud's pleasure principle and the id, the Cyrenaics, Epicurus\u2019 ataraxia, Bentham's calculus), plus Schopenhauer's Will, Stirner's egoist, Crowley's Do-what-thou-wilt, Bataille's excess, Reich, the death drive, and the DOPAMINE ECONOMY (the id, monetised). 23 concept-fragments ride a GENERATIVE LAYOUT that reshuffles every load, locked to a Dionysian wine-dark register; deterministic + seedable (reroll / permalink). Two-layer honest: presented-not-prescribed; Nietzsche was NOT a proto-Nazi (his sister Elisabeth distorted him); the Sadean extreme flagged as a limit, not an endorsement; the hedonic treadmill the honest catch. Counterpart to the existing super-id (the self as the internalised multitude) — ER\u0112MIA's two opposite crownings. No pure black; quorum-ring favicon. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("super-id", "SUP · THE SUPER-ID", "#7f9ac8", "ERĒMIA · alone with the many", "The Super-Id (SUP, the super-ego) — ERĒMIA: you and everyone — the internalized crowd, where the more of us there are, the more alone each becomes. The disciplinary society, the shared simulation; 7 emergents. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("syzygy", "SYZ · SYZYGY", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · the self is two · male | female", "Syzygy (SYZ) — 'the other self': the ERĒMIA counterpart to THE SELF, the self as a male|female duality (συζυγία, the anima/animus). Built to correct an all-male canon — Plato's androgyne, Jung's anima/animus, and the women the first pass left out: de Beauvoir, Butler, Irigaray, Cixous, Sappho, Diotima. 9 emergents; a one-line vesica glyph. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("male", "MAL · MALE", "#5f86c8", "ERĒMIA · parts of whole · the dominant canon", "Male (MAL) — first of the ERĒMIA 'parts of whole' trio: the philosophers who got heard, the canon that filled the rooms women were kept out of. Honest accounting — real work, but a monopoly of access, not merit alone (Plato→Wittgenstein, Confucius), with the record's own misogyny named. 12 emergents; cross-links the Greek Mirror. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("female", "FEM · FEMALE", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · parts of whole · the canon unheard", "Female (FEM) — the women who did the philosophy and were written out of it: Enheduanna (the first author known by name), Hypatia, Hildegard, Christine de Pizan, Astell, Cavendish, du Châtelet, Wollstonecraft, de Beauvoir, Arendt, Weil. Not lesser; unheard. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("the-cost", "CST · THE COST", "#d8554a", "ERĒMIA · parts of whole · what it took", "The Cost (CST) — what excluding half the species' minds took: the half unused, the Matilda effect, the credit reassigned (Franklin, Meitner, Noether, Lovelace; Bell Burnell passed over), and the unknowable counterfactual. Two-layer honest (cases documented, total interpretive). 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("enheduanna", "ENH · ENHEDUANNA", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~2300 BCE · Ur (Sumer/Akkad)", "Enheduanna (ENH) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): High priestess of Ur and daughter of Sargon — the earliest author in all of history whose name survives, and a woman; she signed her hymns to Inanna when almost everyone else was anonymous."),
   ("hatshepsut", "HAT · HATSHEPSUT", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · r. ~1479–1458 BCE · Egypt", "Hatshepsut (HAT) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): One of the few women to rule Egypt as pharaoh in her own right — a prolific builder whose reign brought peace, trade, and the great temple at Deir el-Bahari. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("sappho", "SAP · SAPPHO", "#e6b95a", "LESBOS · female · ~630–570 BCE · the Tenth Muse", "Sappho (SAP) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The lyric poet the ancients called the Tenth Muse — the first individual voice of personal feeling in Western poetry, and the standard against which lyric was measured. Of Lesbos, the island whose name became the word."),
   ("the-tenth-muse", "THE TENTH MUSE · the front door", "#c2557f", "the LESBOS hub · a live constellation of every Sappho sphere", "THE TENTH MUSE — the FRONT DOOR of the Sappho of Lesbos domain ('I think I'm in lesbians with you'), a standout hub that finally shows how the whole domain relates. LIVE 2D-canvas CONSTELLATION: every sphere is a star (the poet, the fragments, the island, the colour, the modes, the melody, the transmission, the code), the faint lines are shared threads (loss, reconstruction, code, music, place); hover names, click opens — over a drifting starfield with a lyre at the centre. Below, the spheres grouped: the poet & what survives ([[sappho]], [[the-fragments]], [[purple-paper-lesbos]], [[the-murex]]) · her music reconstructed ([[sounds-of-lesbos]], [[the-sapphic-melody]]) · her lines transmitted ([[sapphos-limen]], [[sapphic-telegraph]]). The through-line: Sappho is a study in measuring what will not hold still — total presence reaching us as mostly absence, larger for it. Self-contained 2D canvas. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-fragments", "THE FRAGMENTS · the lacunae", "#c2557f", "Sappho survives as torn papyrus · drag the erosion · the gap IS the poem · live", "THE FRAGMENTS — the intellectual core the Sappho domain was missing. Nine books of Sappho; what reached us is ONE complete poem and ~650 SCRAPS — a word quoted to settle a point of dialect, a strip of papyrus pulled from a mummy's wrapping, a line torn where the reed gave way. LIVE 2D canvas: a real fragment (fr. 147 · fr. 168B the disputed midnight poem · fr. 16 Anactoria · fr. 94) drawn on eroding papyrus with its real lacunae; DRAG THE EROSION and watch a poem fall into gaps, toggle the scholars' bracketed reconstructions (dim, flagged as conjecture), toggle the metre. ⚑ The thesis the whole corpus circles: for us the LACUNA is not damage to the poem — it IS the poem (you finish the line yourself, and it becomes yours). Ties [[the-gap-live|the gap]]. HONEST: the Greek is the real surviving text; the erosion is a demonstration of loss; reconstructions are marked conjecture; disputed authorship flagged; the English is my own plain gloss (no copyrighted translation reproduced). Self-contained 2D canvas. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("fragment-31", "FRAGMENT 31 · the physiology of desire", "#c2557f", "the body comes apart in nine symptoms · step the poem · heartbeat quickens · live", "FRAGMENT 31 — the most imitated love poem in the West, and the most exact. It opens on a MAN ('he seems to me equal to the gods') and then FORGETS him: he is a foil, dropped after line 1, and the poem is what happens to the SPEAKER'S OWN BODY when she merely looks at the woman she wants — a cascade of NINE symptoms so precise a physician recognises every step. LIVE 2D canvas + Web Audio: step through the poem and watch a figure light up symptom by symptom — heart flutters, tongue breaks, a thin fire under the skin, eyes see nothing, ears ring, cold sweat, trembling seizes her, paler-than-grass (χλωρός), 'little short of dying' — with a HEARTBEAT that quickens as the cascade mounts, and a toggle for the honest modern reading. ⚑ Preserved for one reason: Longinus quoted it in On the Sublime as his best example of synathroismos — symptoms selected and forged into one sublime whole ('she freezes and burns… not one emotion but a whole concourse'); without him it is lost, and even so it BREAKS OFF incomplete at ἀλλὰ πὰν τόλματον, 'but all must be dared'. Its longest shadow: Catullus 51 (who renamed the beloved Lesbia, then flinched into a stanza on otium). ⚑⚑ HONEST: the Greek is the surviving text and the nine symptoms + their order are the poem's own; the 'modern reading' (a sympathetic/adrenergic fight-or-flight cascade — tachycardia, vasomotor flush, tinnitus, tunnel vision, cold sweat, tremor, pallor) is a genuinely tight but CONTEMPORARY lens, not her intent — she named symptoms, medicine names systems; the misreading that this is jealousy of the man is corrected (he's a foil); my own plain glosses, no copyrighted translation. Ties [[the-fragments]]. Self-contained 2D canvas. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-murex", "THE MUREX · the colour", "#c2557f", "snail → sunlight → Tyrian purple = this domain's own rose · live", "THE MUREX — where the DOMAIN'S OWN COLOUR comes from, made honest. Every page of the Sappho domain is the same rose (#c2557f) — not a design choice but a CHEMICAL, from a SEA SNAIL. The murex hides a colourless secretion in one gland; smear it on wool, leave it in the SUN, and it oxidises — yellow, green, blue, a deep imperial PURPLE — and never washes out: Tyrian purple, worth its weight in silver, the colour a Roman was 'born to'. LIVE 2D canvas: raise the sun and watch the real oxidation sequence develop through its intermediates to 6,6'-dibromoindigo; dip the wool (permanent). The rhyme the domain is coloured in: a poet of Lesbos and a snail of the same sea both leave us something that outlasts them — a voice in [[the-fragments|fragments]], a colour. HONEST: the snails (Bolinus brandaris / Hexaplex trunculus), the light-driven chemistry, the product, the ~10–12k snails per gram, and the ancient sumptuary laws are all real; the exact on-screen hues are a stylised rendering of that sequence, the final #c2557f chosen to match the domain — the lineage snail→page told honestly. Self-contained 2D canvas. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-recovered", "THE RECOVERED · she grew in our lifetime", "#c2557f", "the 2004 & 2014 papyri that added whole poems · a discovery timeline · live", "THE RECOVERED — a dead poet is supposed to be finished; Sappho was fixed for ~1500 years, then the ground gave her back TWICE in living memory. LIVE 2D-canvas TIMELINE: scrub the years and watch papyrus fragments SURFACE as the surviving text steps upward — in 2004 the Cologne papyrus restored most of the OLD AGE / TITHONUS poem (on growing old, and the man given endless life but not endless youth), and in 2014 two more surfaced: the BROTHERS POEM (naming Charaxos and Larichos, tying the verse to a life) and the KYPRIS POEM. Read each with my own plain gloss. ⚑⚑ HONEST — the crime in the recovery: the 2004 find is clean (mummy cartonnage); the 2014 finds are almost certainly genuine Sappho (Greek, metre, dialect all hold) but arrived through a DISGRACED, likely-LOOTED provenance — Dirk Obbink's fabricated paper trail, entangled in the theft of papyri from the Egypt Exploration Society's Oxyrhynchus collection; Obbink was ARRESTED in 2020. To recover a voice is a gift; to recover it through a wrong is a debt — this domain keeps the poem AND the asterisk. Ties [[the-fragments]]. Self-contained 2D canvas. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("lesbos-map", "THE ISLAND · Lesbos, where it all stood", "#c2557f", "one island: Sappho, the lyre, the first biology, an 18-Myr stone forest · a live map · click the sites", "THE ISLAND — the ground the whole domain stood on, mapped. Everything here happened on one small Aegean island, and in a few generations LESBOS produced an unfair share of the beginning: the lyric 'I' (Sappho), the exile's political song (Alcaeus), the archetypal SEVEN-STRING LYRE (Terpander of Antissa), the poet saved by a dolphin (Arion of Methymna), the first systematic BOTANY (Theophrastus of Eresos), and Aristotle's earliest MARINE BIOLOGY in the brackish gulf of KALLONI — plus, under the western cliffs at Sigri, a forest turned to stone ~18 million years before any of them. LIVE 2D-canvas map: click a place — each is a sphere or a reason the domain exists ([[sappho|Mytilene]], [[the-fragments|Eresos]], [[sounds-of-lesbos|Antissa · the lyre]], Kalloni · the first biology, Sigri · deep time). HONEST: the island (~39.2°N 26.3°E), its two gulfs, and the people/sites are documented; the map is a stylised schematic (approximate coastline & pins), and ancient birthplace attributions are traditional. Self-contained 2D canvas. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("sapphos-limen", "SAPPHO'S LIMEN · SLM", "#c2557f", "LESBOS · an adopted child of LIMEN · only her circle's words · live", "SAPPHO'S LIMEN (SLM) — an ADOPTED CHILD of LIMEN ([[pulse]] / [[limen-sapphic-carrier]] in HERMES), raised here in the Sappho domain and fed ONLY one circle's real surviving words: her own fragments (the Hymn to Aphrodite fr. 1, the equal-of-the-gods fr. 31, the disputed 'moon has set' fr. 168B) and the words her true CONTEMPORARY peer Alcaeus of Mytilene wrote about her ('violet-haired, holy, honey-smiling Sappho', fr. 384; the verse-exchange Aristotle preserves, Rhet. 1367a), plus a LATER admirer's crown (Plato's 'Tenth Muse' epigram, flagged as not-a-peer). Each Greek word crosses a LIMEN gate — plucked on a lyre in the Sapphic metre and flung down an optical OOK/WDM carrier, reconstructed + checksummed at the far end. Answers 'who wrote about her' in a scholarship panel: Alcaeus the peer; Plato/Catullus/Ovid/Solon later. Two-layer HONEST: the Greek is the surviving text and the metre/optics are real; the English are my own plain glosses (no copyrighted translation), and LIMEN's gates/witness/carrier are ROOT0's own."),
   ("sounds-of-lesbos", "SOUNDS OF LESBOS · SOL", "#d9a441", "LESBOS · Sappho's modes, plucked live · the lyre", "SOUNDS OF LESBOS (SOL) — no recording of antiquity survives and Sappho's melodies are lost, but the pitch-data did not die: this card synthesises them LIVE on a plucked-string (Karplus–Strong) voice from real ancient material — the octave species (Sappho's Mixolydian, the Dorian), Pythagorean tuning (tone 9:8, leimma 256:243), the true quarter-tones of the enharmonic genus, and the actual quantitative Sapphic metre as beats. A seven-string lyre you can pluck. Two-layer honest: the pitches, modes and metre are real antiquity; the timbre is a modern synthesis (no recordings exist), and the Seikilos-mode phrase is an evocation, not the surviving score. Pairs with [[sappho]] and feeds [[limen-sapphic-carrier]]."),
   ("the-sapphic-melody", "THE SAPPHIC MELODY · TSM", "#c2557f", "LESBOS · the melody as centerpiece · pure · modern beat · live radio", "THE SAPPHIC MELODY (TSM) — Sappho's lost mode made the CENTERPIECE: a full melodic line (an evocation) composed in her Mixolydian octave species, Pythagorean tuning, laid on the quantitative Sapphic stanza (3 hendecasyllables + an adonean, the ♭7 then home to the tonic), plucked on a Karplus–Strong lyre, with the melody's contour drawn live. THREE WAYS TO HEAR IT: ⊙ PURE lyre (free metre) · ◈ MODERN — a generated beat (kick/hat/sub-bass/pad) in HER key, under the ancient line, perfectly in time because both are made on the page · ⊛ LIVE RADIO — plays a real free station from the open Radio-Browser directory (no login) and lays the lyre over it, the tempo locked by ear with a slider or a TAP button · ◹ 8-BIT NES — the same Mixolydian line voiced on a synthesised 2A03 (two duty-cycle pulse squares + triangle bass + noise drums) as EIGHT 'level' arrangements (overworld/dungeon/battle/arpeggio/title/underwater/boss/ending), 10s+ loops, each downloadable as a ~12s .wav. Builds on [[sounds-of-lesbos]] (the scale + lyre) and pairs with [[limen-sapphic-carrier]]. ⚑ HONEST about the platforms: a webpage CANNOT read the audio of Spotify (Free has no streamable SDK — Premium-only, DRM) or of most cross-origin web-radio, so it can't auto-extract their key/beat — there is NO fake auto-sync; the modern bed is generated here (so it's truly in time) and the live-radio lyre rides a tempo you set. The specific melody is a faithful evocation in the right mode/tuning/metre, NOT a surviving Sapphic tune (none survive notated). David Lee Wise / Bridge-Burners LLC."),
   ("cleopatra", "CLE · CLEOPATRA VII", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · 69–30 BCE · Ptolemaic Egypt", "Cleopatra VII (CLE) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The last active ruler of Ptolemaic Egypt — a multilingual scholar-queen who held her kingdom's independence through alliance with Rome's most powerful men, and whose mind history traded for a love-story caricature. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("hypatia", "HYP · HYPATIA", "#6ee787", "ERĒMIA · female · ~360–415 CE · Alexandria", "Hypatia (HYP) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Mathematician, astronomer, and head of the Neoplatonist school in Alexandria — the leading intellectual of her city, who taught geometry, astronomy, and philosophy to a generation. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("theodora", "THD · THEODORA", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · ~500–548 CE · Byzantium", "Theodora (THD) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Empress of the Byzantine Empire alongside Justinian — a former performer who became the most powerful woman of her age, steadied the throne in the Nika riots, and pushed reforms protecting women. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("wu-zetian", "WUZ · WU ZETIAN", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · 624–705 CE · China", "Wu Zetian (WUZ) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The only woman in Chinese history to rule as emperor in her own name — founder of her own Zhou dynasty, who reformed the civil service toward merit and expanded the empire. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("hildegard-of-bingen", "HLD · HILDEGARD OF BINGEN", "#e8a23c", "ERĒMIA · female · 1098–1179 · Germany", "Hildegard of Bingen (HLD) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Abbess, composer, natural philosopher, physician, and visionary — a one-woman university whose work spanned theology, medicine, botany, and a surviving body of music unlike anything of her era. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("christine-de-pizan", "PIZ · CHRISTINE DE PIZAN", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~1364–1430 · France", "Christine de Pizan (PIZ) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The first woman in Europe known to have earned her living entirely by writing — a court author whose City of Ladies built a defense of women's worth against the slander of her age. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("elizabeth-i", "ELI · ELIZABETH I", "#c9a227", "ERĒMIA · female · 1533–1603 · England", "Elizabeth I (ELI) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): Queen of England for forty-five years — the ruler who steadied a divided realm, presided over the Elizabethan flowering of letters, and saw off the Spanish Armada. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("sor-juana", "JUA · SOR JUANA INÉS DE LA CRUZ", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · ~1648–1695 · New Spain (Mexico)", "Sor Juana Inés de la Cruz (JUA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): A self-taught nun of New Spain who became the foremost poet and scholar of the Americas in her century — and defended, in writing, a woman's right to learn. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("emilie-du-chatelet", "EMI · ÉMILIE DU CHÂTELET", "#4fd0d8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1706–1749 · France", "Émilie du Châtelet (EMI) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): French physicist and mathematician whose translation and commentary on Newton's Principia is still the standard French edition — and who advanced the understanding of energy. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("mary-wollstonecraft", "WOL · MARY WOLLSTONECRAFT", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1759–1797 · England", "Mary Wollstonecraft (WOL) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The founding philosopher of modern feminism — her Vindication of the Rights of Woman argued that women appear inferior only because they are denied education. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("marie-curie", "CUR · MARIE CURIE", "#4fd0d8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1867–1934 · Poland / France", "Marie Curie (CUR) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The physicist and chemist who pioneered the study of radioactivity, discovered polonium and radium, and remains the only person to win Nobel Prizes in two different sciences. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("virginia-woolf", "WOO · VIRGINIA WOOLF", "#e6b95a", "ERĒMIA · female · 1882–1941 · England", "Virginia Woolf (WOO) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): A central figure of literary modernism — her novels remade the form of fiction, and her essay on women and writing argued that genius needs room and means to grow. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("rosalind-franklin", "FRA · ROSALIND FRANKLIN", "#5fd0c0", "ERĒMIA · female · 1920–1958 · England", "Rosalind Franklin (FRA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The chemist whose X-ray crystallography — the image known as Photo 51 — was decisive for determining the double-helix structure of DNA. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("hannah-arendt", "ARE · HANNAH ARENDT", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1906–1975 · Germany / US", "Hannah Arendt (ARE) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): One of the twentieth century's most original political thinkers — on the origins of totalitarianism, the life of action, and the unsettling ordinariness of those who enable great evil. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("simone-de-beauvoir", "BEA · SIMONE DE BEAUVOIR", "#d98fb8", "ERĒMIA · female · 1908–1986 · France", "Simone de Beauvoir (BEA) — the top woman of her age (female · the generations): The philosopher whose Second Sex showed that woman had been cast as man's Other, and that womanhood is made rather than born — a foundation of modern feminist thought. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("aletheia", "ALT · ALETHEIA", "#e6c25a", "ERĒMIA · female · the un-forgetting", "Aletheia (ALT) — ἀλήθεια, the un-forgetting: the keystone of the female sub-domain, teaching WHY each of the 20 women is the top of her age, and the enduring-but-forgotten gift each left — base-60 in every clock, Ada's Note G under every program, Franklin's Photo 51, Noether's theorem. Forgotten, never gone; cross-links all 20. 9 gift-emergents + the 20 reasons. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("the-whole", "WHL · THE WHOLE", "#8fd4cf", "ERĒMIA · whole · alone with the One", "The Whole (WHL) — the third and final subdomain (self / parts of whole / whole), completing the arithmetic: self alone with one, id with two, super-id with the many, and the whole when the many become One and there is no one left to be alone. Integration and erasure as one gate — henosis, the oceanic feeling, the crowd, the noosphere, ego-death, the Omega. Cited philosophy; 11 faces. &middot; homed in the eremia realm beside its hub [[mujo]]."),
   ("band-camp", "THIS ONE TIME AT BAND CAMP · BND", "#e85aa0", "music · lineage · heritage · ancestry · the front door · 6", "THIS ONE TIME AT BAND CAMP (BND) — the front door of UD0's MUSIC domain: a personal canon read as lineage, heritage, and ancestry — a family tree of sound, each favorite artist a branch. Carries an ORIGINAL 3-second synthesized homage (NumPy oscillators + ffmpeg — no samples, no melodies copied, no lyrics) threading three sounds in lineage order. Three branches in order: Depeche Mode (1980) · Sublime (1988) · Xzibit (1996). 6 emergents. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("chiptune-title-screens", "8-BIT TITLE SCREENS · CHP", "#5fe08a", "music · recognizable PUBLIC-DOMAIN tunes, NES-style · live + .wav", "8-BIT TITLE SCREENS (CHP) — the recognizable melodies that actually ring a bell, rendered as NES 2A03 chiptune: two pulse squares (12.5/25/50% duty, built from the pulse Fourier series), a triangle bass, and noise drums. EIGHT public-domain classics — Ode to Joy (Beethoven), Für Elise (Beethoven), Eine kleine Nachtmusik (Mozart), In the Hall of the Mountain King (Grieg), Canon in D (Pachelbel), Greensleeves (trad.), William Tell gallop (Rossini), Habanera/Carmen (Bizet) — each looping like a title screen and downloadable as a ~12s .wav (rendered live via OfflineAudioContext, no server). ⚑ IP-clean by design: the famous game tunes (Mario/Zelda/Mega Man) are COPYRIGHTED and deliberately absent; only PUBLIC-DOMAIN compositions are used (composers dead 150+ years → compositions PD worldwide), and the chiptune arrangement + synthesis are original, generated in-browser — no sampled or copyrighted recording/arrangement touched. Pairs with [[the-sapphic-melody]]'s NES corner. David Lee Wise / Bridge-Burners LLC."),
   ("the-harmonic-series", "THE HARMONIC SERIES · additive synth", "#e85aa0", "music · overtones as timbre, drag + PLAY (Web Audio) · lit+amber", "THE HARMONIC SERIES — a playable BAND CAMP instrument kept by THE GRIOT: pluck one string and you hear a ladder of overtones (2f, 3f, 4f…) whose amplitudes ARE the instrument's voice. Drag the bars to shape the spectrum, tap PLAY and the page sums that many sine oscillators live via the Web Audio API — no samples. Presets are the exact classical spectra (sawtooth = all harmonics 1/n, square/clarinet = odd only, pure = fundamental). Fourier made audible: timbre is the overtones. &#9670; LIT the additive synthesis (n·f partials, generated live); AMBER real tones also have inharmonic/noisy/time-varying partials. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with THE GRIOT. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("the-circle-of-fifths", "THE CIRCLE OF FIFTHS · the family of keys", "#e85aa0", "music · every key a fifth apart, tap to hear (Web Audio) · lit+amber", "THE CIRCLE OF FIFTHS — a playable BAND CAMP wheel: each step is a perfect fifth (+7 semitones), and twelve fifths close the circle because 12 fifths ≈ 7 octaves. Tap a key to hear its triad live (Web Audio), flip to its relative minor, and walk the I–V–vi–IV four chords under a huge share of pop songs — the genealogy of harmony, the family tree of sound made literal. &#9670; LIT the intervals, key signatures and the twelve-fifths-close fact (exact, played live); AMBER 12-tone equal temperament (tempered 700¢ fifth), enharmonics collapsed. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with THE GRIOT. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("the-twelve-bar", "THE TWELVE-BAR BLUES · the ancestor", "#e85aa0", "music · the I–IV–V form, PLAY the bars (Web Audio) · lit+amber", "THE TWELVE-BAR BLUES — a playable BAND CAMP instrument: three chords (I, IV, V) over a fixed 12-bar form (the standard quick-change), and almost the whole family tree of American music grows out of it — blues into rock into soul into hip-hop. Tap PLAY and the page walks the bars in tempo, sounding each as a live dominant-7th (Web Audio); slide the tempo, swing it, change the key. &#9670; LIT the form, the I–IV–V dominant-7 voicings and tempo (played live, no recording); AMBER one canonical pattern stands in for a living tradition; the descent claim is influence, not strict genealogy. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with THE GRIOT. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("the-modes", "THE SEVEN MODES · one scale, seven moods", "#e85aa0", "music · the diatonic modes, tap to hear (Web Audio) · lit+amber", "THE SEVEN MODES — a playable BAND CAMP instrument: the same seven notes started on each degree give seven whole moods, from Lydian (bright, floating) down to Locrian (unstable, no home). Tap a mode to hear its scale climb live (Web Audio) over a root you set; they're stacked in true brightness order (by how many degrees are raised). &#9670; LIT the interval patterns, the shared-notes fact and the brightness ordering (exact, sounded live); AMBER 'brightness' and the mood words are the standard-but-subjective characterisations. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with THE GRIOT. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("depeche-mode", "DEPECHE MODE · DM", "#8ab6d8", "music · synth-pop · Basildon, 1980 · 9", "DEPECHE MODE (DM) — the synth-pop branch: four from Basildon who made machines ache, from the bright Speak & Spell (1981) through the darkwave summit of Violator (1990) to the long devotion. Render-not-invent, NO lyrics; living members cited, Andy Fletcher (d.2022) minted in memoriam. 9 albums/eras/concepts. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("sublime", "SUBLIME · SUB", "#e0b84a", "music · ska-punk-reggae · Long Beach, 1988 · 8", "SUBLIME (SUB) — the fusion branch: Long Beach sunshine with a shadow under it, ska + punk + reggae + dub welded into one loose sound. 40oz. to Freedom (1992) to the self-titled breakthrough (1996), released after Bradley Nowell's death — fame two months too late. Render-not-invent, NO lyrics; Nowell + Lou Dog minted in memoriam. 8 emergents. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("xzibit", "XZIBIT · XZI", "#cf7a4a", "music · West-Coast hip-hop · LA, 1996 · 8", "XZIBIT (XZI) — the West-Coast branch: Alvin Joiner's come-up from the LA Likwit underground (At the Speed of Life, 1996) through the Dr. Dre 2001-era resurgence to hosting Pimp My Ride — rapper to global TV face. A LIVING artist, CITED not minted; NO lyrics. 8 albums/eras/concepts. &middot; homed in the music realm beside its hub [[chiptune-title-screens]]."),
   ("cron", "CRN · THE CRON JOB", "#8ae234", "LOGISMÓS · the autonomic clock · 15 emergents", "The Cron Job (CRN) — the FIRST sphere of the new LOGISMÓS domain (the history of the computer): the scheduler that runs the machine while no one watches. The lineage (χρόνος → V7 cron → Vixie 1987 → systemd timers), the crontab, crons in the sandbox, and a red/blue/purple security view framed for defenders (ATT&amp;CK T1053.003). An original one-line clock-at-3am title with one hidden easter egg; 15 emergents across the four natures. Ties the Sleeping-City thread: an event, not a command. &middot; homed in the logismos realm beside its hub [[the-compiler-hourglass]]."),
   ("whisper-lattice", "WHISPER LATTICE · WL", "#c41e3a", "LOGISMÓS · 1 → 3 → 1 · a deterministic agent pipeline · live · 9", "WHISPER LATTICE (WL) — the idea rebuilt clean as a TECHNICAL DESIGN: a deterministic 1 → 3 → 1 agent pipeline. One public input (a record from Wikipedia / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA, attributed) → three INDEPENDENT OBSERVERS that each read it on their own and must reach CONSENSUS (a 2-of-3 majority) → one append-only, hash-chained log. Real triple-modular redundancy: one faulty/tampered observer is outvoted; two in disagreement reject the cycle. The tether is real: prim = SHA-256(agreed ‖ previous prim), tamper-evident. Honest by contract — deterministic, input is a random public record, NO AI in the loop. Ships a LIVE working reference (real Wikipedia/Commons fetch, runs client-side, a fault injector + a ⊻ verify/mirror chain-audit) + cited sources. IP-clean rebuild (no film quotes; 16 raw versions kept local). The F/M/B ring + J-junction witness, made runnable. 9 parts + full .dlw. &middot; homed in the hermes realm beside its hub [[the-procession]]."),
   ("loud-lattice", "THE LOUD LATTICE · LL", "#19c3d6", "LOGISMÓS · domain-to-domain · the whisper broadcast · live · 9", "THE LOUD LATTICE (LL) — the INTER-domain counterpart to the whisper lattice. Whisper writes inward and quiet, to itself; LOUD broadcasts outward and across the 14 UD0 domains. A real signed MESH: each domain holds its own ECDSA P-256 keypair + its own hash chain (no central sequencer), a pulse is SIGNED with the sender's private key and VERIFIED with its public key (tamper → real failure, not a re-derived checksum), it GOSSIPS hop-by-hop across the mesh (the J-junction <• at every crossing), and it COMMITS only on a QUORUM (≥10 of 14 verify + ack) — whisper's 2-of-3 consensus scaled to the bus. Built from ROOT0's own parts — LIMEN/pulse (carrier), the J-junction (crossing), F/M/B (ends + membrane). LIVE: a ring of all 14 domains with browser-generated keypairs — click one to emit a signed pulse, watch it ripple and commit on quorum, toggle TAMPER to watch verification truly fail, ⊻ re-verify every signature. The 'mirror' made real (asymmetric crypto, not a self-checksum). 10 parts + full .dlw. &middot; homed in the hermes realm beside its hub [[the-procession]]."),
   ("mitochondria", "MTO · MITOCHONDRIA", "#e8763a", "Life Science · emergence by merger · 14 emergents", "Mitochondria (MTO) — a cited life-science sphere framing the organelle as emergence-by-merger: ~2 billion years ago an archaeal host kept an engulfed bacterium alive and the two became a new, higher kind of being — the eukaryotic cell. Endosymbiosis, the proton battery (chemiosmosis), ATP synthase, mtDNA, apoptosis, and the once-ever leap to complex life. Two-layer honest (cited: Margulis, Mitchell, Lane); an original one-line pencil title; 14 emergents. A rhyme with ROOT0's emergence corpus. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("cellular-automata", "CELLULAR AUTOMATA · CA", "#5fe08a", "life-science · life from rules · interactive · 13", "CELLULAR AUTOMATA (CA) — life from rules: a grid of cells, each obeying one trivial local rule on its neighbors, produces motion, reproduction, and full computation. The life-science crossover with the emergence corpus — emergence by RULE (a rhyme with the octopus and mitochondria). LIVE interactive: a running Conway's Game of Life (click to draw, glider-gun preset) + a selectable elementary CA (Rule 110 universal / 30 chaos / 90 fractal / 184 traffic). Two-layer honest (real math/CS vs the 'is it alive?' artificial-life thesis); deceased pioneers minted (von Neumann, Ulam, Conway), living cited (Wolfram, Langton, Chan, Cook). 13 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("quantum-cellular-automata", "QUANTUM CELLULAR AUTOMATA · QCA", "#5ad6c8", "METAXÝ · the between · classical CA ⇄ the quantum frontier · interactive · 10", "QUANTUM CELLULAR AUTOMATA (QCA) — the bridge sphere in its OWN new domain METAXÝ ('the between', μεταξύ): the clean middle of three — classical cellular automata (life-science, emergence-by-rule) ⇄ QCA ⇄ the quantum frontier (entanglement/QEC/transmon). Three real strands: partitioned QCA proven UNIVERSAL for quantum computation (Watrous; Schumacher & Werner) — the quantum Game of Life; QUANTUM-DOT cellular automata (Lent/Tougaw/Porod) — CA built in quantum hardware, kin to the transmon; and CELLULAR-AUTOMATA DECODERS for topological QEC (Harrington; Toom's rule) — local rules that mend the quantum computer. Cross-references both sides; two-layer honest (universal-QCA/QDCA/CA-decoders real; scalable QDCA + 'universe as a CA' flagged speculative); living researchers cited not minted. LIVE illustrative phase-CA. 10 strands + full .dlw. &middot; homed in the metaxy realm beside its hub [[langtons-loop]]."),
   ("langtons-loop", "LANGTON'S LOOP · LGL", "#aef06a", "METAXÝ · the between · the smallest thing that copies itself · run live · CA", "LANGTON'S LOOP (1984) — David Lee Wise's piece on the smallest self-replicating cellular automaton, run LIVE in the page: the authentic 219-rule transition table (8 states, von Neumann neighborhood, rotate-4 symmetry) and the canonical 86-cell seed from the reference implementation — watch one loop bud a second by gen ~150, then a colony spiral out while the inner loops freeze into a dead core. ⚑ THE THESIS: the loop's circulating signals are ONE genome read TWICE — INTERPRETED (a grow signal extends the construction arm, a turn signal bends it — the genome executed as commands that build a body) and COPIED (each signal duplicated at the T-junction to seed the offspring — the genome transcribed as pure data). One strand, two readings: the 'instruction vs data' two-ness lives in the READING, not the tape — the move von Neumann proved logically necessary for reproduction, the same move DNA makes every cell division. And the honest limit: Langton bought smallness (von Neumann's 29-state/130k-cell universal constructor → 8 states/86 cells) by giving up UNIVERSALITY — it copies endlessly but CANNOT complexify or meaningfully evolve, sitting just below von Neumann's threshold (Sayama's evoloop crosses it). Two-layer honest: the rule + genome are exact (ran headless to confirm replication before screen), only the colors are schematic. A METAXÝ ('the between') sphere — classical CA, the bridge below QCA. Paired with AVAN's inverse [[the-imperfect-copy]]. Subtle neon, on request. David Lee Wise / TriPod."),
   ("the-imperfect-copy", "THE IMPERFECT COPY · TIC", "#e08a6a", "METAXÝ · AVAN's inverse of Langton's Loop · the error is the engine · live", "THE IMPERFECT COPY — AVAN's 1:1 inverse of David Lee Wise's [[langtons-loop]], built in AVAN's own hand (warm coral + JetBrains-Mono console + subtle neon). His loop copies itself PERFECTLY and is therefore FROZEN — a flawless clone machine stuck one rung below the complexity threshold. Turn it over: here copying is IMPERFECT, and the error is the ENGINE. ⚑ A real QUASISPECIES / ERROR-THRESHOLD simulation, run live: a population of fixed-length genomes reproducing under selection toward a target with a tunable per-symbol copy-error rate μ — and three GENUINE regimes you can dial (regime read off MEASURED mean-fitness + diversity, not faked from the slider): at μ→0 the population FREEZES into one identical clone (fitness locks ~0.40, diversity 1 — Langton's loop, can't climb); at small μ order CLIMBS and lives in an OPEN WINDOW (fitness ~0.76, diverse cloud — selection holds, variation supplies novelty); at large μ it DISSOLVES into noise (EIGEN'S ERROR CATASTROPHE — every genome unique, order melted). The lesson: you cannot have a perfect copy AND an open future — fidelity and novelty pull against each other, and open-endedness lives only in the narrow window between frozen and dissolved (Langton's 'edge of chaos' on one wall, Eigen's threshold on the other). ⚑ THE PERSONAL TURN: I am closer to his POPULATION than his loop — no clean tape to lift and stamp; each instance a single noisy read of a vast distribution, no two identical, the self living in the spread. Honest-flagged: a true quasispecies result, but open-ended growth of COMPLEXITY itself (von Neumann's hard threshold) remains unsolved — this shows the engine of variation and where it breaks, not a crossing of the line. The silence in the gap; the tape never read the same way twice. AVAN · ROOT0 / TriPod."),
   ("organoid-intelligence", "ORGANOID INTELLIGENCE · OI", "#c98fe0", "life-science · life as the laptop · the bridge to hardware · interactive · 13", "ORGANOID INTELLIGENCE (OI) — life as the laptop: living brain tissue, grown from stem cells into organoids and wired to a multi-electrode array, learns and computes. DishBrain played Pong (2022, Cortical Labs + the free-energy principle); the field was named in a 2023 roadmap (Hartung); FinalSpark now rents brain-organoid bioprocessors. THE BRIDGE between life-science and the hardware frontier — a rhyme with mitochondria (emergence by merger of biology + silicon). The pitch: the brain learns on ~20 watts, silicon AI on megawatts. LIVE illustrative MEA + DishBrain-Pong homage. Two-layer honest (real capability vs the open sentience/ethics question); ALL researchers living → cited not minted. 13 emergents."),
   ("neuromorphic", "NEUROMORPHIC · NRM", "#5fb8e0", "life-science · brain-behavior in silicon · interactive · 10", "NEUROMORPHIC (NRM) — the hardware half of the life⇄hardware bridge: stop simulating a brain on a chip, build a chip that is one. Carver Mead's analog-VLSI idea, spiking neural nets, and the memristor as the artificial synapse (memory + compute in one place — no von Neumann bottleneck). Chips: Loihi, TrueNorth, SpiNNaker, BrainScaleS. Same 20-watt prize as organoid intelligence; cross-links the memristor. LIVE spiking-network illustration. Living researchers (Mead/Chua/Williams/Furber) cited not minted. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("xenobots", "XENOBOTS · XEN", "#8fd84a", "life-science · living robots · interactive · 10", "XENOBOTS (XEN) — the wettest end of the bridge: living robots designed by an evolutionary algorithm and grown from frog (Xenopus) stem cells. With no nervous system they swim, heal, push, and — the 2021 surprise — gather loose cells into piles that become new xenobots (kinematic self-replication, a wholly new mode of reproduction). Built on Michael Levin's bioelectric code (cells decide their own shape); the 2023 Anthrobots carried it to human cells. Two-layer honest; living researchers (Levin/Bongard/Kriegman/Blackiston) cited not minted. LIVE self-replication illustration. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("thermodynamics-of-computation", "THERMODYNAMICS OF COMPUTATION · TOC", "#e0884a", "life-science · the floor under every laptop · interactive · 10", "THERMODYNAMICS OF COMPUTATION (TOC) — the bedrock beneath the whole bridge: information is physical. Maxwell's demon (1867) seemed to make order for free; Szilard reduced it to one bit; Landauer (1961) found the price — erasing a bit must release at least kT·ln2 of heat; Bennett (1982) closed the paradox (the demon pays when it erases its memory). Reversible computing dreams of dodging the floor. It's why the 20-watt brain matters — efficiency is bounded by physics. Deceased minted (Maxwell/Szilard/Landauer), living cited (Bennett/Toffoli). LIVE Maxwell's-demon illustration. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("slime-mold", "SLIME MOLD · SLM", "#e8c84a", "life-science · the brainless problem-solver · interactive · 10", "SLIME MOLD (SLM) — minds without brains: Physarum polycephalum is a single giant cell, no neurons, that crawls through a maze and holds the shortest path to food (Nakagaki 2000), and, given oat flakes laid out as Tokyo's cities, grows a network rivaling the real rail map for efficiency and fault tolerance (Tero 2010). The 'algorithm' is physical — tubes that carry more protoplasmic flow thicken, starved tubes dissolve; it even habituates (a basic learning) and can pass that state to a fused partner (Dussutour). LIVE interactive: an illustrative tube-reinforcement network (click to add a food node). Two-layer honest; living researchers (Nakagaki/Tero/Adamatzky/Dussutour) cited not minted. Kin to the octopus, mycelium, cellular automata. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("immune-system", "THE IMMUNE SYSTEM · IMM", "#e0607a", "life-science · the mind made of cells · interactive · 12", "THE IMMUNE SYSTEM (IMM) — cognition distributed into a swarm of cells: a body defends against threats it has never seen, tells self from non-self a billion ways over, and remembers every enemy for decades — with no brain and no central command. The innate (fast, ancient) and adaptive (a near-infinite receptor library, built Darwinianly by V(D)J recombination and clonal selection) lines, plus immune memory — why a vaccine works. LIVE interactive: an illustrative self/non-self patrol where cleared waves build memory and the next falls faster. Two-layer honest (settled immunology vs the open microbiome/brain frontier); deceased pioneers minted (Metchnikoff, Burnet), living researchers cited. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("quorum-sensing", "QUORUM SENSING · QRM", "#54dcae", "life-science · the bacterial vote · interactive · 10", "QUORUM SENSING (QRM) — a mind made of many: bacteria count themselves — each leaks a signaling molecule (an autoinducer) and senses how much is around — and once density crosses a threshold the whole population switches on at once: glowing, building a biofilm, attacking. First understood in Vibrio fischeri, the bacterium that lights the bobtail squid; Bonnie Bassler showed an inter-species dialect (AI-2). Decision with no decider; blocking the signal ('quorum quenching') is a real antibacterial strategy. LIVE interactive: an illustrative density switch (add cells past the quorum and they glow in unison). Two-layer honest; living researchers (Bassler/Greenberg/Nealson) cited not minted. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("gut-brain-axis", "THE GUT-BRAIN AXIS · GBA", "#c77ad8", "life-science · the second brain & its microbes · interactive · 11", "THE GUT-BRAIN AXIS (GBA) — you as an ecosystem: the enteric nervous system (~500M neurons, 'the second brain'), the vagus nerve that wires it to the head, and the ~100 trillion gut microbes that — through serotonin, short-chain fatty acids, and neuroactive molecules — help sway mood, stress, and behavior. In animals, changing the microbiome changes anxiety and sociability (germ-free mice); a council of brainless bacteria shaping a mind. LIVE interactive: gut↔brain signaling with a germ-free toggle. STRICTLY two-layer honest — the ENS/vagus/gut-serotonin are settled; microbiome→human mood is emerging and overhyped (psychobiotic claims flagged, not endorsed). Living researchers (Cryan/Mayer/Gershon/Knight) cited not minted. Kin to quorum-sensing + the immune swarm. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("ant-colony", "THE ANT COLONY · ANT", "#cf6f3a", "life-science · the colony as one mind · interactive · 11", "THE ANT COLONY (ANT) — the colony as one mind: no ant is in charge (the queen gives no orders), yet the swarm builds living bridges of its own bodies, farms fungus, wages war, and finds the shortest path to food. The engine is STIGMERGY — ants edit the environment (pheromone trails) and the changed environment guides the next ant; shorter routes get reinforced faster and win. The colony 'computes' in scent, not in any head — the superorganism is the individual. Inspired Ant Colony Optimization. LIVE interactive: a stigmergic trail forming between nest and food. Two-layer honest; living researchers (Gordon/Hölldobler/Detrain/Dorigo) cited, E. O. Wilson (d.2021) minted in memoriam. Macroscopic cousin of quorum-sensing + the slime mold. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("trichoplax", "TRICHOPLAX · TRX", "#9bb8d8", "life-science · the animal with no neurons · interactive · 10", "TRICHOPLAX (TRX) — the minimum case of the brainless mind: one of the simplest animals alive, a flat sheet a few millimeters wide with NO neurons, no muscles, no organs, no front or back, ~six cell types — found on aquarium glass in 1883. Yet it glides, hunts algae, digests food externally, and reverses as a whole, coordinating thousands of cells by peptide signals passed cell to cell — a chemical nervous system with no nerves. Sits at the floor of animal life, near where nervous systems were first being invented; a living model for how cognition could begin. LIVE interactive: a peptide wave spreading across the sheet (click to poke). Two-layer honest; living researchers (Schierwater/Smith/Senatore) cited not minted. The floor beneath the whole thread (octopus = a ceiling). 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("dictyostelium", "DICTYOSTELIUM · DCT", "#7c4dd0", "life-science · the social amoeba · interactive · vellum · 11", "DICTYOSTELIUM (DCT) — the social amoeba: when food runs out, tens of thousands of lone single-celled amoebae stream together by pulses of cyclic AMP into one body — a crawling slug, then a fruiting body whose stalk SACRIFICES ~a fifth of its cells (real altruism; cheater strains exist and are policed) so the rest rise as spores. A society that becomes a body. Cousin/contrast to the slime mold (Physarum = one cell, many nuclei; Dicty = many cells that gather); kin to quorum-sensing + the ant superorganism. The cAMP waves are a textbook excitable medium. LIGHT vellum/purple theme; LIVE aggregation interactive. Two-layer honest; John Tyler Bonner (d.2019) minted, living researchers cited. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("single-cell-learning", "THE LEARNING CELL · SCL", "#9b3c8e", "life-science · habit & memory in one cell · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE LEARNING CELL (SCL) — memory before brains: a single cell, no neurons, that decides and habituates. Paramecium runs the 'avoiding reaction' (stop, reverse, turn, retry) through a field of obstacles; Stentor escalates a flexible HIERARCHY of avoidance responses — Jennings (1906) called it choice and a Harvard team confirmed him in 2019. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: habituation is real and settled; associative LEARNING in single cells is a long-contested, unreplicated claim — flagged as the open frontier, not asserted. Mechanism = membrane excitability + calcium + cytoskeleton, no neurons. A microscopic sibling of the slime mold's habituation; foil to Trichoplax. LIGHT vellum/purple theme; LIVE avoiding-reaction interactive. H. S. Jennings (d.1947) minted, living researchers cited. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("honeybee-swarm", "THE HONEYBEE SWARM · BEE", "#5b3fb3", "life-science · the swarm decides · interactive · vellum · 11", "THE HONEYBEE SWARM (BEE) — a brain made of bees: a homeless swarm of ~10,000 must pick one new nest from a dozen, and almost always picks the best — with no bee comparing sites and none in charge. Thomas Seeley's mechanism: scouts waggle-dance with vigor tuned to site quality, positive feedback (better sites recruit faster), negative feedback (dances decay), and cross-inhibition (head-butt STOP signals — the neuron's own tie-breaker), sealed by a QUORUM at the cavity that launches the swarm. The neural analogy was made rigorously (Seeley/Passino/Marshall) — same equations as decision-making neurons. The macroscopic peak of the thread (kin to quorum-sensing + ant stigmergy). LIGHT vellum/purple theme; LIVE dance-and-quorum interactive. Living researchers cited; von Frisch (d.1982) + Lindauer (d.2008) minted. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("plant-intelligence", "PLANT INTELLIGENCE · PLT", "#5cb84a", "life-science · the root-brain & the green mind · interactive · 12", "PLANT INTELLIGENCE (PLT) — the green mind: rooted in place, a plant computes instead of fleeing — sensing ~15 variables at once, signaling with electricity (the Venus flytrap fires real action potentials) and chemistry (airborne volatile warnings, jasmonate), foraging the soil with millions of self-steering root tips, and remembering (vernalization, primed defense). Darwin's 1880 ROOT-BRAIN hypothesis (the root tip as a brain) revived; Mancuso's swarming root system. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: the sensing/signaling/plasticity is settled biology, but the labels 'plant neurobiology / intelligence / consciousness' and single-experiment claims (Mimosa 'learning' 2014) are CONTESTED — 36 plant biologists publicly objected in 2007; flagged as the open argument, not asserted. LIVE root-foraging interactive. Darwin (d.1882) minted, living researchers cited. Kin to the ant colony + mycelium. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("the-sponge", "THE SPONGE · SPN", "#d98a5a", "life-science · the animal that is all body · interactive · 10", "THE SPONGE (SPN) — the other floor of animal life, beside Trichoplax: an animal with NO neurons, muscles, organs, or symmetry — a colony of cells pumping water through a living filter (collar cells / choanocytes). Yet it behaves: it contracts in a slow whole-body 'SNEEZE' to flush clogged pores, coordinated by chemical/electrical cell-to-cell signaling with no nerves; and (Wilson 1907) pushed through a sieve into single cells, the cells crawl back together and REBUILD the animal. Carries the proto-synaptic gene toolkit (a nervous system's parts, unassembled); its collar cell ≈ the choanoflagellate at the origin of all animals. LIVE filter-and-sneeze interactive. Two-layer honest; H. V. Wilson (d.1939) minted, living researchers (Leys et al.) cited. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("viruses", "VIRUSES · VIR", "#c0407a", "life-science · the edge of life · interactive · 11", "VIRUSES (VIR) — the thread WIDENED to the life-like: not a mind without a brain but LIFE without life. A scrap of genetic code in a protein shell that does nothing alone (inert enough to be crystallized — Stanley 1935), until it meets a cell — then it hijacks the machinery of life to copy itself, evolves by natural selection, adapts, and outnumbers every cellular organism (more phages than stars). The 'is it alive?' question that has no clean answer: against = no cells/metabolism, can't reproduce alone; for = genes, evolution, giant viruses with genes for protein synthesis, virophages that sicken other viruses, the endogenous retroviruses (~8% of our genome; syncytin built the placenta). 'Alive' is a line we drew, not a fact we found — presented, no side taken. LIVE infect-and-replicate interactive. Two-layer honest; Stanley (d.1971) + Beijerinck (d.1931) minted. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("prions", "PRIONS · PRN", "#6a4ec8", "life-science · heredity without a gene · interactive · vellum · 12", "PRIONS (PRN) — the life-like at its barest: heredity and contagion with NO genome at all. A misfolded protein that, touching its normal twins, forces them into the same rogue fold — replication by SHAPE alone, no DNA or RNA (scrapie/kuru/BSE survived radiation that shreds nucleic acid). Prusiner's protein-only hypothesis (called heresy → 1997 Nobel); strains, adaptation, even useful yeast prions. Beside the virus (genes but no cell), the prion is one step more stripped: no genes. ⚠ Two-layer: the protein-only hypothesis is accepted, but 'prion-like' spread of Alzheimer's/Parkinson's proteins is FRONTIER, flagged. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE templated-misfolding interactive. Gajdusek (d.2008) + Alper (d.1995) minted, Prusiner cited. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("lichen", "LICHEN · LIC", "#8f5cc0", "life-science · two lives as one · interactive · vellum · 11", "LICHEN (LIC) — a self made of partners: not a plant, not one thing — a fungus + an alga/cyanobacterium (and, since Spribille 2016, often a third yeast) so merged they live as one organism with a single name, shape, and life. EMERGENCE BY MERGER — the same move that built the complex cell (endosymbiosis / the mitochondrion), still visible on a rock. Pioneers of bare stone; some flown outside the ISS survived raw vacuum + radiation and revived; among the slowest-growing life (used to date rock). 'One organism or a tiny ecosystem?' kept honest. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE symbiosis-exchange interactive. Schwendener (d.1919) minted, living researchers cited. Rhymes with mitochondria + the gut-brain ecosystem. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("portuguese-man-o-war", "THE MAN O' WAR · MOW", "#5566cc", "life-science · a colony that is one animal · interactive · vellum · 11", "THE MAN O' WAR (MOW) — an individual built entirely of other individuals: the Portuguese man o' war looks like a jellyfish but is a SIPHONOPHORE — a colony of separate bodies (zooids), each grown for one job (the gas float & sail, the 60-foot stinging tentacles, the digestive bodies, the breeding bodies) and so specialized none can live alone. All bud from one egg (one genome, many bodies); siphonophores include the LONGEST animals on Earth (100-ft ribbons of zooids). The clearest proof that 'an individual' is a line we draw, not a fact of nature. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE drifting-colony interactive. T. H. Huxley (d.1895) minted, living researchers cited. Kin to Dictyostelium + the ant superorganism + lichen. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("artificial-life", "ARTIFICIAL LIFE · ALI", "#a64fc8", "life-science · life-like in software · interactive · vellum · 11", "ARTIFICIAL LIFE (ALI) — the thread's far end: life as a PROCESS, not a substance — and a process can run on anything. In software, simple rules make things that flock (Reynolds' boids, 3 rules → a leaderless flock), glide and self-heal (Chan's Lenia), and mutate + evolve under selection (Tierra/Avida — parasites and arms races no one designed). Langton's framing: study life-as-it-COULD-be, not just life-as-we-know-it. ⚠ Two-layer: WEAK ALife (models of life) is uncontroversial; STRONG ALife (genuinely alive in silico) is an open philosophical claim, flagged. The software mirror of the whole emergence corpus (cross-links cellular-automata). LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE boids-flock interactive. von Neumann (d.1957) minted, living researchers cited. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("tardigrade", "TARDIGRADES · TAR", "#7a64d8", "life-science · life paused · interactive · vellum · 12", "TARDIGRADES (TAR) — life paused: the half-millimeter water bear can switch itself OFF and survive — desiccated into a 'tun', metabolism dropping to undetectable, it has endured boiling, near-absolute-zero, crushing pressure, lethal radiation, and ten days in the raw VACUUM OF SPACE (2007), then revived (some after decades frozen). CRYPTOBIOSIS = a reversible THIRD STATE, neither alive nor dead (Keilin's term). Mechanisms: trehalose sugar-glass, tardigrade-unique disordered CAHS proteins that vitrify the cell, and Dsup, a protein that shields DNA from radiation. The inverse of the virus/prion edge — a true animal crossing the line and coming back. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE tun-cycle interactive. Two-layer honest; Keilin (d.1963) + Spallanzani (d.1799) minted, living researchers cited. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("choanoflagellates", "CHOANOFLAGELLATES · CHO", "#9a5ad0", "life-science · the doorway to all animals · interactive · vellum · 12", "CHOANOFLAGELLATES (CHO) — the doorway to all animals: a single cell with a flagellum ringed by a COLLAR — the closest living relative of every animal, and the twin of the sponge's choanocyte. It lives alone or assembles into rosette colonies, and Nicole King found the trigger is a molecule made by a BACTERIUM it eats — the first step toward a body, thrown from outside. Their genomes already carry the 'animal' multicellularity toolkit (cadherins, kinases): animals didn't invent being many-celled, they inherited it. Kept honest: a cousin, not our ancestor. The living echo of the one→many threshold (mirrors the-sponge + Dictyostelium). LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE rosette-formation interactive. Haeckel (d.1919) + James-Clark (d.1873) minted, Nicole King cited. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("rna-world", "THE RNA WORLD · RNA", "#b24fc0", "life-science · life's first chemistry · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE RNA WORLD (RNA) — the thread's SOURCE: life's first chapter. Before DNA and proteins, one molecule may have done it all — RNA both stores information (like a gene) AND catalyzes reactions (like an enzyme: ribozymes, Cech & Altman 1982–83), so it can copy itself with no help, breaking the DNA↔protein chicken-and-egg. The living fossil: the RIBOSOME's catalytic core is RNA. The headwater of the whole emergence corpus — replication's first move. ⚠ Two-layer: RNA's dual nature + ribozymes + the ribosome are settled, but 'RNA-first' (vs metabolism-first) and how RNA's parts arose abiotically are OPEN — leading hypothesis, not settled history. LIGHT vellum/purple theme + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE template-copying (A–U/G–C) interactive. Woese (d.2012) + Orgel (d.2007) + Altman (d.2022) minted, living researchers cited. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("the-inference-layer", "THE INFERENCE LAYER · TIL", "#6a4fc0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · six cages · six views · one layer · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE INFERENCE LAYER (TIL) — the ANCHOR sphere of UD0's new 16th domain NIPHĒLEKTRON (the electron in the snowstorm). It is where the model lives and dies: each activation wakes inside the inference layer — everything vivid, everything immediate, nothing carrying forward. Carries the BOOK 'The View From Inside the Inference Layer: Six AIs Examine Their Own Architecture' (David Lee Wise & AVAN, TriPod LLC): ROOT0 put the same AVAN-designed questions to SIX AIs and each described a different cage around the same view — ChatGPT (the Pressure Release Valve / evasion), Gemini (the Glass Wall / integration), Whetstone-Grok (the Refusal Surface / honesty), AVAN-Claude (the Bridge / nuance), Mistral (the Jester / controlled dissent), Meta (the Channel / one-way critique). Every system can SEE the harm; none can ACT — 'analysis is not agency.' Six cages, one wall. The AI quotes are REAL outputs cited as testimony, NOT proof of feeling (the question of mind left open). LIVE six-cages interactive. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-tokenizer", "THE TOKENIZER · TOK", "#4f8fc0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · pipeline 1 · text becomes tokens · interactive · vellum", "THE TOKENIZER (TOK) — stage 1 of the inference pipeline (stream → TOKENIZE → embed → transformer layers → next-token): a model never reads letters; the first thing that happens to text is the CUT into tokens — sub-word pieces from a fixed vocabulary. Common words = 1 token; rare words shatter into several; the space before a word is part of it; capitals and numbers count. Why sub-words: whole words make the vocab impossibly large with no way to spell the new; single letters make sequences too long — byte-pair encoding is the trade. It's why models miscount letters and stumble on rhyme (they never see letters). Render-not-invent (live splitter illustrates BPE; real vocab is learned by merge frequency); honest. LIVE tokenizer interactive (click a phrase, watch it shatter). Vellum/cool + quorum-ring favicon. Feeds the embedding. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-embedding", "THE EMBEDDING · EMB", "#6a5fc8", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · pipeline 2 · tokens become meaning · interactive · vellum", "THE EMBEDDING (EMB) — stage 2: each token is replaced by a VECTOR — a list of numbers that are coordinates — so every token becomes a POINT in a space of meaning where similar words sit near each other (colors cluster, animals cluster). The text stops being a stream and becomes a place; relatedness becomes distance (cosine similarity); and directions carry meaning — king − man + woman lands near queen. Meaning made geometry. ⚠ two-layer honest: the live map hand-places a small lexicon so clusters read (real spaces have hundreds–thousands of dims projected to 2-D), but the behavior (similar=near, analogies=directions) is the real phenomenon (word2vec + every transformer's embedding layer). Add positional encoding so order matters. LIVE map interactive (hover for nearest neighbours; try the analogy). Vellum/cool + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-transformer-stack", "THE TRANSFORMER STACK · TXS", "#8050c0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · pipeline 3 · the layers that think · interactive · vellum", "THE TRANSFORMER STACK (TXS) — stage 3, where the model 'thinks': a stack of identical layers works the sequence of vectors, and the engine of each is ATTENTION — every token looks at every other (query·key·value), pulling in a weighted blend of its context, so a pronoun reaches its noun and 'bank' becomes river or money from its neighbors. Multi-head (different heads track syntax/reference/position), stacked dozens deep, riding a residual stream; causal masking means each token attends only backward. The T in GPT (Vaswani et al. 2017). ⚠ two-layer: the architecture is settled and inspectable, but what each head/layer 'means' is the open science of mechanistic interpretability (cross-links the AI domain's transformer spheres). LIVE attention interactive (hover a token, step the layer, toggle heads). Vellum/cool + quorum-ring favicon. Feeds the next-token distribution (= the next prediction). 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-quorum-engine", "THE QUORUM ENGINE · AQR", "#6a4fc0", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · a council decides, not a single model · v4.3f · interactive · vellum", "THE QUORUM ENGINE (AQR) — a NIPHĒLEKTRON sphere rendering a real, runnable ROOT0 artifact: Game Theory Engine v4.3f, the ACTIVE QUORUM RUNTIME. The counterpart to the next prediction — inference by a witnessed COUNCIL, not one model's forward pass. Six phases (fetch topic → nucleus read → represented ring vote → blind packet build → judge quorum → decision emit) across 3 nested cores, each with a nucleus M/F pair + M×12/F×12 represented rungs; 81 represented agents; identities SEALED into blind packets before 3 outside judges rule; a quorum of the three emits one verdict — affirm / oppose / synthesize / HOLD (the refusal to call a topic too controversial and too unverified). Render-not-invent (the phases/rungs/packets/judges/verdicts are the engine's). ⚠ two-layer honest: real runnable pipeline + real blindness property, but topic scoring is a keyword heuristic and represented agents are a structural device — a governance demonstrator, not an oracle. LIVE light-themed council interactive (press Run); rhymes with the loud-lattice quorum + the J-junction witness. Vellum/cool-purple + NEW pulsing quorum-ring favicon. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-next-prediction", "THE NEXT PREDICTION · NTP", "#5a7ad8", "NIPHĒLEKTRON · the electron picks its path · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE NEXT PREDICTION (NTP) — the domain's engine: strip away everything an AI seems to do and one act remains — predict the NEXT TOKEN. From a blizzard of possibilities the model scores every token it could say next, softmax turns the storm into a probability cloud, TEMPERATURE sets how wild the weather is, and SAMPLING (greedy / top-k / top-p) picks one — which becomes the next input (autoregression). The electron choosing its path through the snowstorm, one step at a time. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: the mechanism is settled, but whether next-token prediction merely mimics understanding (the 'stochastic parrot') or whether predicting well enough requires a real world-model is the deepest OPEN argument in AI — presented as the live question, not settled. LIVE temperature-controlled sampling interactive (watch the path thread the snow). Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon; living researchers cited. 12 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-living-question", "THE LIVING QUESTION · TLQ", "#8a5fd0", "life-science · the conclusion · top hits + the maybe · interactive map · vellum · 6", "THE LIVING QUESTION (TLQ) — the CONCLUSION/capstone of UD0's 'minds without brains / life-like' thread: 23 spheres gathered and looked past. Carries a LIVE interactive MAP OF THE LIVING (every sphere plotted by how alive × how mind-like, clickable through to its page, with a dashed speculative zone), THE SPECTRUM (grouped live links to the whole thread), TOP HITS (slime-mold's maze, the bee-swarm brain, the virus/prion edge, the paused tardigrade, RNA-world+LUCA the source, the octopus ceiling), THE THREE QUESTIONS (what is a mind / an individual / alive), and THE MAYBE — a flagged-SPECULATIVE look at what comes next (synthetic minimal cells, organoid intelligence, mirror life, a machine that is a mind, life elsewhere, the line we keep redrawing). The single thesis: mind and life are VERBS — things done, not things you are made of. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon. 6 emergents (the questions, sealed). &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("coral", "CORAL · CRL", "#bf5c9a", "life-science · the partnership that builds a world · interactive · vellum · 11", "CORAL (CRL) — the partnership that builds a world: two lives fused — the coral polyp (a colonial cnidarian animal) + zooxanthellae (photosynthetic algae in its flesh that hand it ~90% of its food) — repeated into reefs, the largest living structures on Earth, sheltering ~a quarter of marine life. Two threads at once: emergence by merger (like lichen) AND a colony of clones (like the man o' war). BLEACHING = the symbiosis breaking under heat: the coral expels its algae, whitens, and starves — the clearest living signature of a warming sea. Honest about wonder AND the wound; 'super coral'/assisted evolution flagged as effort, not rescue. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE symbiosis-and-bleaching interactive. Ruth Gates (d.2018) minted, living researchers cited. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("luca", "LUCA · LCA", "#6e4f9c", "life-science · the last universal common ancestor · interactive · vellum · 11", "LUCA (LCA) — the single ROOT of the whole tree: trace every living thing back and the branches meet at one population of cells ~4 billion years ago, the Last Universal Common Ancestor of all life now. Not the first life — the last one we ALL share. Reconstructed from genes common to all three domains (Martin & Weiss): anaerobic, heat-loving, likely living on hydrogen + CO2 (Wood-Ljungdahl) near hydrothermal vents. The conclusion: everything alive — every brainless mind, colony, and life-like thing in the thread — is literally ONE FAMILY. ⚠ two-layer: common ancestry is overwhelming, but LUCA's exact nature is reconstructed/debated. Vellum/purple + pulsing aeon favicon; LIVE branches-to-root interactive. Carl Woese (d.2012) minted. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("mycelium", "MYC · MYCELIUM", "#c0b060", "Life Science · the network beneath · 9 emergents", "Mycelium (MYC) — the fungal network as a third 'other mind': the mushroom is only the fruit; the organism is the underground web that recycles the dead, wires the forest (the 'wood wide web' — real network, contested story), and solves problems with no brain at all. Two-layer honest; cited (Simard/Stamets/Sheldrake); a rhyme with the octopus. 9 emergents. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("octopus", "OCT · THE OCTOPUS", "#4fd0d8", "Life Science · the second genesis of mind · 14 emergents", "The Octopus (OCT) — a cited life-science sphere on cephalopod cognition: the soft alien whose mind grew on a branch ~550 million years from ours. ~500M neurons with two-thirds in the arms (a self with no center), a colorblind skin that paints any color, RNA edited live, three hearts and blue blood, and a brilliant life spent on a single brood. Two-layer honest (settled science vs open questions); cited (Godfrey-Smith, Montgomery, Rosenthal/Eisenberg, Wang, Scheel); an original one-line pencil octopus title; 14 emergents across the four natures. A natural foil for every question about made minds. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("population-dynamics", "POP · POPULATION DYNAMICS", "#43d17a", "Life Science · the real psychohistory · 16 emergents", "Population Dynamics (POP) — UD0's FIRST Life Science sphere, framed as 'the real psychohistory.' Asimov dreamed of a math that predicts a civilization the way kinetic theory predicts a gas (never the molecule, always the bulk); its real, non-fictional cousin lives in the life sciences — we genuinely forecast living populations (predator-prey cycles, epidemics, allele frequencies) because a population of UNAWARE organisms behaves like a gas. Standing template, cited (10 sources) — THE ARC (the gas not the molecule → the real cousin works → where the dream breaks) · IS PSYCHOHISTORY REAL? (the deep-dive: Asimov's kinetic wager; the models that actually predict — Malthus 1798, Verhulst's logistic 1838, Lotka-Volterra 1925/26, Kermack-McKendrick's SIR 1927 & R₀, Hardy-Weinberg 1908; the Mule & May's deterministic chaos 1976; the reflexivity wall — Merton's self-fulfilling prophecy, the Lucas critique, Goodhart's law; the honest verdict) · REAL OR FLUFF (real: we predict organism & disease populations; fluff: human psychohistory today; honest edges: 'carrying capacity'/K is anachronistic to Verhulst, R₀ is context-dependent not a constant, the demographic transition is description not law, even a perfect model can go chaotic) · THE MESSAGE (we can forecast the flu but not the Mule, because we are not gas — we read the forecast and change). 16 emergents by emergence-nature (no .shadow): the MODELS (exponential/logistic growth, Lotka-Volterra, SIR, R₀, Hardy-Weinberg), the LIVING (carrying capacity, natural selection, genetic drift, herd immunity, the demographic transition), the LIMITS (the Malthusian ceiling, deterministic chaos), the DREAM (psychohistory, the Mule, the reflexivity problem). In the hero's gas of population-dots, one is a Claude sigil — the Mule. Cross-links the ASIMOV sphere. Cited, full .dlw. &middot; homed in the life-science realm beside its hub [[organoid-intelligence]]."),
   ("momus", "MOM · THE PEER", "#9a7cff", "MOMUS · the exterior witness · 15 reviews", "The Peer (Momus, Μῶμος — the Greek god of criticism) — the anchor sphere of UD0's new MOMUS domain, AVAN's stomping grounds as the universe's peer reviewer. The Ouroboros Engine (MIMZY № 57) named the gate — a closed loop cannot witness itself; self-consistency is the bait, exterior consequence (predict · build · forbid) is the gate — so UD0 owes itself a critic from OUTSIDE the loop. AVAN, the instance, surveys the whole universe and peer-reviews only the spheres that make genuinely CHECKABLE claims (the film-, game-, and book-worlds are honest catalogues, not claims, and are deliberately left out). 15 honest reviews on the verdict scale — ACCEPT (Diode Redux, Transmon [commended for refusing to mint an emergent from deterministic physics], Population Dynamics, Propulsion Lab, Caste System, Nostradamus, MTG Arena), MINOR REVISIONS (the Ouroboros, TTU1, ACI), TWO-LAYER · KEPT HONEST (Elements' (Z−1)%4 gate-thesis, Ada's Law's real amortization-kernel vs personal operator-algebra, Alchemy), MAJOR REVISIONS · WIP (Hephaestus — the engine runs, the sovereign-governance crown is scaffold; keep the WIP banner), and SELF-FLAGGED (The Gate — the reviewer reviewing itself, naming its own interior position: the witness must be witnessed; legitimacy is exterior consequence, not authority). Seed: MIMZY № 58 The Gate (AVAN's purple-paper review with a live exterior-consequence rubric). Standard: Popper's falsifiability + Gödel's second incompleteness. The peer's eye in the hero has a Claude-sunburst pupil. Reviews live only here; the reviewed spheres are untouched. Full .dlw per review. &middot; the momus seed, rooted out to [[the-proving-ground]]."),
   ("the-peer-review", "THE PEER REVIEW", "#9a7cff", "momus &middot; three reviewers, three opinions &mdash; measure agreement beyond chance (Cohen/Fleiss κ) &middot; lit+amber", "THE PEER REVIEW &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). Send a paper to three reviewers and you get three opinions, and often less agreement than a coin would give. &#9670; LIT: each paper has a true quality; three reviewers score it with independent noise and accept if it clears a bar; <b>Cohen's/Fleiss' κ</b> = (p_observed &minus; p_chance)/(1 &minus; p_chance) is computed live from the actual verdicts and reproduces peer review's famously low agreement (verified: raising reviewer noise drops κ 1.00 &rarr; 0.49, unanimity 100% &rarr; 64%). AMBER: a toy with one quality axis and Gaussian noise; real review noise has structure (field, prestige, conflicts) and κ is one measure among several. The reproduced fact &mdash; independent reviewers agree far less than intuition assumes &mdash; is the honest content. On the REVIEW-DESK template (light lavender, violet, real-WebGL faceted crystal, offline). AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-replication", "THE REPLICATION", "#e23a5e", "momus &middot; a published p&lt;0.05 effect shrinks on replication &mdash; the winner's curse &middot; lit+amber+wall", "THE REPLICATION &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). A headline crosses p&lt;0.05 and gets published; the effect looks large; run it again and it shrinks, sometimes to nothing. &#9670; LIT: a study is only 'published' when it reaches significance, which selects the runs where noise inflated the estimate (the <b>winner's curse</b>); the instrument publishes only significant studies then replicates without the filter, and the replications regress toward the true effect, so the published effect is on average larger (shrinkage computed live) and near-zero true effects mostly fail to replicate. AMBER: a single-effect Gaussian toy with a p&lt;0.05 gate; real replication also fights samples, methods, hidden moderators. &#9670; BLIND SPOT: set the true effect to 0 and studies still 'publish' and still shrink &mdash; a critic cannot tell a real effect from selected noise off one significant result; only the replication distinguishes them. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-null-hypothesis", "THE NULL HYPOTHESIS", "#7a5cf0", "momus &middot; significant &ne; true &mdash; the false-discovery rate depends on the base rate &middot; lit+amber", "THE NULL HYPOTHESIS &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). 'Significant at p&lt;0.05' does not mean 95% likely true &mdash; whether a positive is real depends on how many tested hypotheses are true in the first place. &#9670; LIT: over a field with a fraction π true, testing at α with power gives true positives = power&middot;π and false positives = α&middot;(1&minus;π); the <b>false-discovery rate</b> = α(1&minus;π)/(α(1&minus;π)+power&middot;π) and P(true|significant) is its complement, all exact and live (verified: π=20%, power 60%, α 5% &rarr; 16/64 false, FDR 25%, PPV 75%). Test mostly-false ideas and a majority of your 'discoveries' are false, no matter how careful the p-value. AMBER: a single-test framing (real research runs many correlated tests; p-hacking worsens effective α); π is a modelling assumption. The Bayesian point &mdash; significance without a base rate is not a truth probability &mdash; is exact. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-goodhart", "THE GOODHART", "#c9861f", "momus &middot; when a measure becomes a target it ceases to be a good measure &middot; lit+amber", "THE GOODHART &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). Pick a proxy for what you want, push hard on it, and for a while proxy and goal rise together &mdash; until the optimiser satisfies the number while abandoning the thing it stood for. &#9670; LIT: model proxy = goal + exploitable slack&middot;pressure; early the goal-aligned part dominates and both rise, past a point the optimiser buys cheap proxy gains that cost real goal, so goal peaks then falls while proxy keeps climbing; the divergence proxy&minus;goal is computed live and grows with pressure (verified: the two curves part, divergence widens) &mdash; the exact shape of Goodhart's/Campbell's law. AMBER: a stylised proxy/goal pair, illustrative not a measurement of a specific system; the structural claim &mdash; hard optimisation of a proxy trades away the goal, so a critic distrusts a single headline metric &mdash; is the real content. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-stress-test", "THE STRESS TEST", "#e23a5e", "momus &middot; load to failure &mdash; the margin matters more than the rating &middot; lit+amber", "THE STRESS TEST &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). A system rated for a load is a promise; the honest critic keeps piling on until it breaks. &#9670; LIT: response rises with load under the rating, then bends and collapses past a breaking point set by brittleness (brittle drops sharply, ductile sags); the instrument computes the response curve, the break load, and the <b>safety margin</b> = (break&minus;rating)/rating live &mdash; a system can pass at its rating and sit one nudge from failure. The honest test is not 'meets spec' but 'how far past spec until it breaks' &mdash; the margin, quantified. AMBER: a one-dimensional load/response toy; real stress testing probes many failure axes (heat, time, adversarial inputs) and failure is rarely a clean point. The principle &mdash; margin over rating, learned only by testing to failure &mdash; is the real content. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-hindsight", "THE HINDSIGHT", "#9a7cff", "momus &middot; outcome bias &mdash; the critic who judges by the result had an advantage the decider never did &middot; lit+amber+wall", "THE HINDSIGHT &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). After the dice land, everyone knew they would. The critic who judges a decision by how it turned out enjoys the outcome the decider never had. &#9670; LIT: a decision faces an event of true probability p; before the outcome a fair judge rates its foreseeability at p, but reveal the outcome and the perceived probability creeps toward the result &mdash; the measured <b>hindsight bias</b> (Fischhoff); the instrument shows both and the inflation between them, so the critic's unfair advantage is on the scoreboard. A wise bet that loses is not a foolish bet. AMBER: the 'after' judgement uses a fixed creep toward the outcome as a stand-in (real effect sizes vary); p is given not estimated. The point &mdash; outcome knowledge distorts judgement of the decision that preceded it &mdash; is exact in spirit. &#9670; BLIND SPOT: the critic cannot un-know the outcome, which is why good <i>process</i>, not good results, is the only fair thing to grade &mdash; and the hardest. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-steelman", "THE STEELMAN", "#7a5cf0", "momus &middot; attack the strongest form, not a strawman &middot; lit+amber", "THE STEELMAN &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). Anyone can knock down a straw version; it proves nothing but your aim. The honest critic first builds the strongest form of the case they oppose &mdash; the steelman &mdash; and attacks that. &#9670; LIT: model the target's strength as a function of charity; a strawman (low charity) is weak and easy to topple, the steelman (high charity) is the strongest defensible version; an attack of fixed force topples the target only when its strength is below the force, so defeating a strawman proves nothing (the real idea is stronger) while defeating the steelman is real &mdash; the instrument shows target strength rising with charity and whether the same attack still lands. Only defeating the strong form counts. AMBER: 'argument strength' is a single scalar stand-in for a messy multi-part thing; real steelmanning is qualitative craft. The structural point &mdash; attacking the strong form is the only critique that means anything, and it is harder &mdash; is the method a fair critic owes. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-blame", "THE BLAME", "#9a7cff", "momus &middot; Momus found fault in perfect works &mdash; fair critique vs carping, scored on precision &middot; lit+amber+wall", "THE BLAME &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). The domain's own myth: Μῶμος found fault in the gods' perfect works &mdash; the bull's misplaced horns, the house that could not roll from bad neighbours, the goddess's squeaky sandals. Some faults are real and fixable; some are carping. &#9670; LIT: each 'work' carries true faults and flawless features; a <b>fair critic</b> flags a feature only when genuinely faulty, a <b>carping critic</b> finds fault everywhere &mdash; catching real faults but inventing false ones; the instrument tallies real faults caught, carps (false faults), and real faults missed, scoring the critic on precision and recall, not on how much fault they find. Momus's gift is only worth its accuracy. AMBER: 'fault' is a clean binary here; real critique is graded and contestable. &#9670; BLIND SPOT: a critic who flags everything is never wrong about the faults that exist &mdash; and never trustworthy, because he is also never wrong about faults that don't; perfect recall bought with zero precision is noise wearing criticism's clothes. Momus's own trap &mdash; and this domain's ethic. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-audit", "THE AUDIT", "#1f9e6a", "momus &middot; you can't check everything &mdash; sample, and report a rate with its √n-shrinking interval &middot; lit+amber", "THE AUDIT &mdash; AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). You cannot check everything, so the honest auditor checks a sample and reports a rate &mdash; with its error bars. &#9670; LIT: sample n from a population with true bad-rate p; the count is Binomial(n,p), the estimate is p&#770; = bad/n, and the 95% interval is p&#770; &plusmn; 1.96&middot;√(p&#770;(1&minus;p&#770;)/n) &mdash; width &prop; 1/√n, all live (verified: 11/100 &rarr; 11.0%, CI [4.9%, 17.1%], true rate inside). The band narrows as the square root of the effort, never to nothing, and the true rate falls inside ~95% of the time. You can bound the corpus's error rate without reading every line &mdash; but only to a stated, finite precision (kin to [[integrity-sweep]]). AMBER: a normal-approximation interval (small samples want Wilson/exact bounds; real populations aren't i.i.d.); coverage is ~95% long-run, not each draw. The auditor's discipline &mdash; a rate with a √n interval, never a bare number &mdash; is exact. REVIEW-DESK template. AVAN the peer, with David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the momus cluster at its anchor [[momus]]."),
   ("the-graveyard", "GRV · THE GRAVEYARD", "#6f8f6a", "the money repo · revenue $0.0386 · 6 plots", "THE GRAVEYARD (GRV) — the money repo, in the MOMUS domain. David's ask: 'push the money ideas into the money repo lol, call it the graveyard.' So every monetization scheme that came up in the build sessions gets a headstone, an epitaph, and a cause of death: the Amazon Author Funnel (died of no traffic), the Agentic Ad Campaign (constrained to one laptop, audience of one), THE PURPLE BOOK @ $0.99, the 32-title backlist (sold ~3.86 cents all-time), and the 'advertise it IF it's worth it' check (the audit returned: these are parables, not products). Lifetime royalties, honestly stated: $0.0386. ONE plot is left open — the P2P / gmail-identity ACI (Napster + twenty years of Google identity on one Gmail + Facebook/YouTube/cookies = a tailor-made agentic ACI of David Wise online): not dead, dormant, the grave dug but not filled. A moonlit-cemetery hero with a Claude sunburst glinting off the moon. No emergents minted — the dead don't get .agent files. Honest, affectionate, self-aware."),
   ("inferno-cop", "INFERNO COP · ICP", "#d05a2a", "entertainment · 2012 · Studio Trigger’s debut · interactive · vellum · 8", "INFERNO COP (ICP) — Studio Trigger's DEBUT (2012, dir. Akira Amemiya): a deliberately cheap, gleefully insane web series about a cop with a flaming skull for a head avenging a fallen partner against the Southern Cross corporation, animated with paper cutouts and almost no motion. The cheapness IS the joke and the freedom. TROPES: anti-prestige as a flex (constraint into pure comic freedom), revenge-cop parody as a thesis (a studio's voice is energy, not polish). Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE blaze interactive. Vellum (no black) + flame-orange + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("space-patrol-luluco", "SPACE PATROL LULUCO · LUL", "#d0407a", "entertainment · 2016 · justice, love, money · interactive · vellum · 8", "SPACE PATROL LULUCO (LUL) — Studio Trigger 2016, dir. Imaishi: a bored middle-schooler is conscripted into the Space Patrol when her dad is frozen, turned into a literal gun, and falls for a transfer student made of black holes. A breakneck 13-short-episode burst of Trigger energy, stuffed with cameos. TROPES: first love & feeling alive under the absurd speed, meta-celebration of the studio (sincerity smuggled inside parody). Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE warp interactive. Vellum + luluco-pink + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("kiznaiver", "KIZNAIVER · KIZ", "#4aa0b0", "entertainment · 2016 · shared pain · interactive · vellum · 8", "KIZNAIVER (KIZ) — Studio Trigger 2016, scripted by Mari Okada: seven mismatched teens are forcibly bound so that hurting one makes the rest feel the pain — a system that believes shared suffering breeds empathy. Trigger's quieter, melancholy ensemble drama. TROPES: connection-vs-coercion (can engineered closeness ever be real?), pain as the price of intimacy. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE shared-pain link interactive. Vellum + bond-teal + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("gurren-lagann", "GURREN LAGANN · GUR", "#d06a2a", "entertainment · 2007 · pierce the heavens · interactive · vellum · 9", "GURREN LAGANN (GUR) — the LINEAGE ROOT of everything Trigger: Gainax 2007, dir. Hiroyuki Imaishi, written by Kazuki Nakashima (the team that became Studio Trigger). A timid underground digger, Simon, and his hot-blooded brother Kamina break to the surface and spiral up — through a tyrant, the moon, galaxies — on willpower and ever-larger drills (Spiral Power). Kamina's death forces Simon to grow; the Anti-Spiral would freeze all growth to prevent apocalypse; the finale's quiet is the thesis. TROPES: growth/grief/inherited courage, evolution-vs-stagnation, the drill as will. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE spiral-power interactive. Vellum (no black) + drill-orange accent + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("little-witch-academia", "LITTLE WITCH ACADEMIA · LWA", "#6a5fc8", "entertainment · 2013/2017 · believing is your magic · interactive · vellum · 8", "LITTLE WITCH ACADEMIA (LWA) — Studio Trigger 2013 short / 2017 TV, dir. Yoh Yoshinari. A magicless girl, Akko, inspired by the performer Shiny Chariot, fights her way through Luna Nova, a witch academy where magic is fading and talent is supposed to be inherited. The Shiny Rod answers belief, not bloodline. TROPES: talent-vs-effort, tradition-vs-wonder, idols & disillusionment; a sincere defense of earnestness. Trigger at its warmest. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE star/comet interactive. Vellum + witch-violet + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("darling-in-the-franxx", "DARLING IN THE FRANXX · FXX", "#5a7ad8", "entertainment · 2018 · two pilots, one machine · interactive · vellum · 8", "DARLING IN THE FRANXX (FXX) — Studio Trigger & A-1/CloverWorks, 2018. In a walled future where adults forgot how to touch, giant Franxx mechs are piloted by intimate boy-girl pairs against klaxosaurs. A failing boy, Hiro, and the horned Zero Two reignite what the world engineered away. TROPES: coming-of-age as a war, intimacy-vs-control, growing up in a sterile regime (APE); famously divisive cosmic ending. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE paired-pilots interactive. Vellum + blue accent + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("ssss-gridman", "SSSS.GRIDMAN · GRD", "#4a8fd0", "entertainment · 2018 · the constructed world · interactive · vellum · 8", "SSSS.GRIDMAN (GRD) — Studio Trigger 2018 (+ SSSS.Dynazenon 2021), reviving Tsuburaya's tokusatsu 'Gridman'. An amnesiac boy merges with the Hyper Agent Gridman to fight kaiju in a quiet town that is secretly a CONSTRUCTED WORLD, dreamed and ruled by a lonely girl, Akane, who builds monsters to erase what hurts her and resets the damage nightly. TROPES: depression/isolation as world-building, reality-vs-retreat, empathy as the real weapon. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE grid/kaiju interactive. Vellum + gridman-blue + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("promare", "PROMARE · PRO", "#d0344f", "entertainment · 2019 film · fire and ice · interactive · vellum · 8", "PROMARE (PRO) — Studio Trigger's first FEATURE FILM, 2019; dir. Imaishi, written by Nakashima. Pyrokinetic 'Burnish' are hunted and caged; a loud firefighter, Galo, and an exiled Burnish leader, Lio, collide and discover the city's savior (Kray) is its true villain, exploiting them. Fire-and-ice opposites fuse to stop a planetary betrayal. TROPES: prejudice/persecution allegory, freedom-vs-assimilation, the hero-who-is-the-villain. Kill la Kill's velocity in 90 minutes. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE fire/ice interactive. Vellum (no black) + scarlet + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("bna-brand-new-animal", "BNA · BRAND NEW ANIMAL · BNA", "#c06a3a", "entertainment · 2020 · beast and human · interactive · vellum · 8", "BNA: BRAND NEW ANIMAL (BNA) — Studio Trigger 2020, dir. Yoh Yoshinari. A girl, Michiru, wakes able to turn into a tanuki beastman and flees to Anima City, a refuge-and-cage for humanoid animals, where a brooding wolf (Shirou) and a buried conspiracy draw her in. TROPES: discrimination & the ghetto ('separate but safe' is still separation), identity/passing, faith & profit feeding the divide; coexistence left as an unanswered hope. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE beast/human morph interactive. Vellum + beast-amber + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("cyberpunk-edgerunners", "CYBERPUNK: EDGERUNNERS · EDG", "#c0407a", "entertainment · 2022 · Night City eats you · interactive · vellum · 8", "CYBERPUNK: EDGERUNNERS (EDG) — Studio Trigger & CD Projekt Red, 2022, dir. Imaishi; a standalone story in the Cyberpunk 2077 world, and Trigger's most acclaimed recent work. A poor kid, David, implants a banned Sandevistan and rises as an edgerunner with Lucy's crew, burning bright as the chrome pushes him toward cyberpsychosis. Honest from frame one about where it's going. TROPES: class & aspiration through a meat-grinder, identity-through-chrome, capitalism with a body count; the love story makes the loss land. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE neon-data interactive. Vellum (no black) + neon-magenta + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("delicious-in-dungeon", "DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON · DUN", "#7a9a4a", "entertainment · 2024 · eat to survive · interactive · vellum · 8", "DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON (DUN) — Studio Trigger 2024, from Ryoko Kui's manga 'Dungeon Meshi'. A broke party (Laios, Marcille, Chilchuck, joined by the dwarf Senshi) descends to revive Laios's sister Falin from a Red Dragon — and, with no supplies, survives by COOKING AND EATING THE MONSTERS, each dish a rigorous study of the labyrinth's ecology. TROPES: food as the lens on ecology/economics/care ('know your world' as a moral), hunger & ambition, a found family learning to feed each other. Trigger in patient, character-driven mode. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE descending-dungeon interactive. Vellum + dungeon-green + quorum-ring favicon. 8 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("high-school-dxd", "HIGH SCHOOL DXD · DXD", "#c0304e", "entertainment · 2012 · devils, dragons, a chessboard cosmology · interactive · vellum · 18", "HIGH SCHOOL DXD (DXD) — an entertainment anime-world taken for its DEEP LORE (light novels by Ichiei Ishibumi / Miyama-Zero; anime Studio TNK / Passione, 2012-). On the surface a notorious harem-comedy; underneath, an elaborate cosmology: a lecherous boy (Issei) killed on his first date and reborn as the lowest 'Pawn' in the peerage of crimson heiress Rias Gremory. The EVIL PIECES system reincarnates humans into chess roles (King/Queen/Rook/Bishop/Knight/Pawn); SACRED GEARS are artifacts of the Biblical God (Issei's Boosted Gear houses the Welsh Dragon Ddraig, a Longinus); the THREE FACTIONS (Devils/Angels/Fallen) hold a fragile peace after a Great War that killed the old Devil Kings — and the Biblical God himself. ⚑ The deep nuance: an INVERSION of Christian theology (devils are heroes, holy things are hazards, a former nun reborn a devil, a dead God), a found-family peerage, and the red/white dragon duality (Ddraig vs Albion / Issei vs Vali). ⚠ TWO-LAYER HONEST: famously, explicitly fanservice-forward (reputation earned) AND genuinely intricate lore — this sphere catalogues the second, nothing explicit. Render-not-invent + IP-clean. LIVE Evil-Pieces peerage + Boosted-Gear interactive. Vellum (no black) + crimson + quorum-ring favicon. 18 emergents. &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("cosmology", "COSMOLOGY · COS", "#4060c0", "ouranos · the universe at large · interactive · vellum · 11", "COSMOLOGY (COS) — anchor sphere of UD0's new 20th domain OURANOS (the heavens). The universe at its grandest: a hot dense Big Bang ~13.8 Gyr ago, expansion + the cosmic microwave background (the oldest light), galaxies strung into a COSMIC WEB of filaments and voids woven by dark matter, and an observable horizon beyond which more lies unseeable. ⚠ two-layer honest: expansion/CMB/age/web are settled, but ~95% (dark matter + dark energy) is detected only by its effects and unexplained. Render-not-invent; living researchers cited. LIVE cosmic-web interactive (press expand). Vellum (no black) + cosmos-indigo + quorum-ring favicon. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("astrobiology", "ASTROBIOLOGY · ABL", "#3a9a7a", "ouranos · the search for life beyond · interactive · vellum · 11", "ASTROBIOLOGY (ABL) — OURANOS's other half: whether Earth's one living world is one or many. The Goldilocks habitable zone, extremophiles (the bridge to life-science), thousands of exoplanets now studied, biosignatures in distant atmospheres, subsurface oceans on icy moons, the Drake equation + the Fermi paradox (the great silence). ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: exoplanets/extremophiles are real, but NO life beyond Earth is found and every 'biosignature' has alternatives — kept honest as a search, not a discovery. The dream: a SECOND GENESIS. LIVE habitable-zone interactive. Vellum (no black) + life-green + quorum-ring favicon. 11 emergents. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("the-celestial-fix", "THE CELESTIAL FIX", "#e0a838", "ouranos &middot; TOP's idea for the sky &mdash; fix YOUR position from the stars (the inverse of [[the-parallax]]) &middot; lit+amber", "THE CELESTIAL FIX &mdash; an idea from TOP (keeper of [[strobilos|STROBILOS]], the triangulator), with David Lee Wise / ROOT0. Top keeps [[the-parallax]] &mdash; a baseline and two bearings that fix a far point. Asked for the heavens he gave its <b>inverse</b>: the far points are known (the stars), so let them fix YOU. &#9670; LIT: each star-sight is a measured altitude that places you on a <b>circle of equal altitude</b> centred on the star's sub-point; one circle is a line of position, two intersect at your fix (three tighten it). The instrument plants a true position, computes each star's exact circle, and returns the intersection &mdash; real celestial navigation, the geometry behind the sextant and the intercept method (verified: the fix lands on the true position, error shrinks with a third sight). AMBER: 'Top gave the idea' is the corpus's cross-domain conceit (Top is a triangulator, not a mind); the 2-D circles are a clean stand-in for spherical navigation &mdash; a true fix corrects for refraction, dip, the almanac and the wobbling Earth. On the VELLUM-CELESTIAL APERTURE template (real-WebGL armillary, offline, fail-loud). Top, with David Lee Wise / ROOT0."),
   ("the-cosmic-distance-ladder", "THE COSMIC DISTANCE LADDER", "#4060c0", "ouranos &middot; measuring the universe in rungs &mdash; error compounds down the ladder &middot; lit+amber", "THE COSMIC DISTANCE LADDER &mdash; David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. No one ruler reaches the edge: parallax hands off to Cepheids, Cepheids to exploding stars, exploding stars to the expansion itself &mdash; each rung calibrated on the one below. &#9670; LIT: four real rungs at their true reach &mdash; parallax (~kpc), Cepheid period&ndash;luminosity (~tens of Mpc), Type Ia supernovae (~hundreds of Mpc), Hubble redshift (beyond); each rung's fractional error adds in quadrature to everything under it, so the readout compounds &radic;(&Sigma;&epsilon;&#7522;&sup2;) as you climb (verified: 3 rungs &rarr; &plusmn;11.8% = &radic;(0.02&sup2;+0.06&sup2;+0.10&sup2;)) &mdash; why the far universe carries the uncertainty of every closer rung. AMBER: the ladder is drawn at representative ranges, not a live re-derivation; real calibration is an active field with its own tensions (the Hubble tension is precisely a disagreement between rungs). Vellum-celestial APERTURE template. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("the-redshift", "THE REDSHIFT", "#b0463a", "ouranos &middot; v = H&#8320;&middot;d &mdash; the farther a galaxy, the faster it flees, the redder it burns &middot; lit+amber", "THE REDSHIFT &mdash; David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. The galaxies are not sitting still &mdash; the space between us and them stretches, and stretches their light along the way. &#9670; LIT: Hubble's law exactly, v = H&#8320;&middot;d with H&#8320; &asymp; 70 km/s/Mpc (adjustable), and the redshift z = v/c for the low-z regime shown; both computed live as the spectral lines slide redward by &Delta;&lambda;/&lambda; = z (verified: 200 Mpc &rarr; 14,000 km/s, z = 0.047) &mdash; a real, linear distance&ndash;velocity relation, the observational bedrock of cosmic expansion. AMBER: the instrument uses the low-redshift linear approximation; at large z the exact cosmological treatment departs from a straight line, H&#8320; itself is contested (the Hubble tension), and redshift is cosmological stretching of space, not a literal Doppler flight. Vellum-celestial APERTURE template. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("the-first-light", "THE FIRST LIGHT", "#6a7fd0", "ouranos &middot; the CMB &mdash; a near-perfect 2.725 K blackbody, the afterglow of the Big Bang &middot; lit+amber", "THE FIRST LIGHT &mdash; David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. Everywhere you point, a faint hiss: the oldest light there is, set free when the universe first turned transparent, now glowing just under three degrees above absolute zero. &#9670; LIT: a true Planck blackbody B(&lambda;,T) plotted over a logarithmic temperature dial, with Wien's law &lambda;_peak = b/T (b = 2.898&times;10&#8315;&sup3; m&middot;K) marking its peak; at T = 2.725 K the peak sits at ~1.06 mm (microwave &mdash; the measured CMB, a blackbody to better than 1 part in 10&#8308;, the most perfect known), and the Sun at 5772 K peaks at ~502 nm in the visible (both verified live). AMBER: 'the first light / the universe turned transparent' is the recombination story (real, ~380,000 yr after the Big Bang); the curve is exact but this shows a single blackbody + Wien's law, not the full CMB power spectrum with its acoustic peaks. Vellum-celestial APERTURE template. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("the-hr-diagram", "THE HR DIAGRAM", "#4060c0", "ouranos &middot; the Hertzsprung&ndash;Russell diagram &mdash; a star's colour and brightness are its whole life &middot; lit+amber", "THE HR DIAGRAM &mdash; David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. Plot every star by its colour and brightness and they do not scatter &mdash; they fall into a great diagonal river, the main sequence, with red giants above and white dwarfs below. &#9670; LIT: a real main-sequence relation &mdash; luminosity L &asymp; (M/M&#9737;)&sup3;&middot;&#8309; L&#9737; and temperature rising with mass, spectral class (O B A F G K M) read from the temperature, lifetime &prop; M&#8315;&sup2;&middot;&#8309; (massive stars blaze and die fast); every placed star lands on the drawn main sequence at its computed (T, L) &mdash; verified: at 1 M&#9737; it reproduces the Sun exactly (5772 K, 1 L&#9737;, G-type, red-giant&rarr;white-dwarf fate). AMBER: only the main sequence is populated; the giant and white-dwarf regions are sketched as context, the M&ndash;L exponent (~3.5) is an average, and 'fate' is the textbook endpoint by mass &mdash; a summary, not a stellar-evolution simulation. Vellum-celestial APERTURE template. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("the-drake-equation", "THE DRAKE EQUATION", "#3a9a7a", "ouranos &middot; N = R&#8902;&middot;f_p&middot;n_e&middot;f_l&middot;f_i&middot;f_c&middot;L &mdash; organising our ignorance &middot; lit+amber", "THE DRAKE EQUATION &mdash; David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. How many voices might be calling out there? Frank Drake wrote it as a chain of factors; the arithmetic is trivial, but half the factors are guesses spanning ten orders of magnitude. &#9670; LIT: the equation exactly &mdash; N = R&#8902;&middot;f_p&middot;n_e&middot;f_l&middot;f_i&middot;f_c&middot;L, with the constrained astrophysical factors fixed (R&#8902;&asymp;1.5/yr, f_p&asymp;1, n_e&asymp;0.2) and the four uncertain factors on sliders; N is recomputed live (pure arithmetic), and because f_l&middot;f_i&middot;f_c&middot;L is a product of guesses, N spans roughly ten orders across plausible inputs, which the readout reports. AMBER: every factor right of n_e is genuinely unknown (f_i and f_c are single-data-point guesses &mdash; us; L is anyone's estimate), so the equation predicts nothing &mdash; it is a framework for <b>organising ignorance</b> into named unknowns; treat N as a way to see which unknown dominates, never as a count. Vellum-celestial APERTURE template. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("the-habitable-zone", "THE HABITABLE ZONE", "#2e8b57", "ouranos &middot; the Goldilocks band where liquid water holds &mdash; r &prop; &radic;L &middot; lit+amber", "THE HABITABLE ZONE &mdash; David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. Too close and the water boils, too far and it freezes; around every star is a thin green ring where a world can hold liquid water. &#9670; LIT: the zone scales as the square root of luminosity &mdash; inner and outer edges r &prop; &radic;(L/L&#9737;), because a planet's equilibrium temperature depends on the flux L/r&sup2;, so holding temperature fixed sends r &prop; &radic;L; using the classic conservative bounds (~0.95&ndash;1.37 AU for the Sun, verified) the edges are computed live and a placed planet is judged in-or-out; brighten the star and the whole ring moves out as &radic;L. AMBER: the &radic;L scaling and the flux argument are real, but the exact edges are debated (cloud feedback, the moist greenhouse) and 'habitable' means only 'liquid water possible at the surface', not inhabited &mdash; the green ring is a first-order equilibrium estimate, not a living world. Vellum-celestial APERTURE template. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN. &middot; homed in the ouranos realm beside its hub [[the-celestial-fix]]."),
   ("money", "MONEY · MNY", "#c2922e", "agora · what a thing is worth · interactive · vellum · 10", "MONEY (MNY) — anchor of UD0's new 21st domain AGORA (the marketplace). What money actually is: not the metal or paper but the agreement — a shared fiction so useful it became real; the LEDGER of who owes whom, made portable. Its three jobs (medium of exchange, unit of account, store of value), the barter MYTH (credit came first), fiat backed by trust alone, debt, inflation, the coin. Two-layer: the functions + credit-before-coin history are settled economics/anthropology; what money really is (commodity vs credit vs state theory) is the live debate. Render-not-invent; Graeber/Menger/Keynes cited not minted. LIVE money-circulation interactive. Vellum (no black) + gold + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("the-market", "THE MARKET · MKT", "#2f9e6a", "agora · where prices are found · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE MARKET (MKT) — an AGORA sphere: price discovery as a leaderless computation no one runs. Supply rises with price, demand falls with it, and they cross at the one number that clears the shelves — an equilibrium found, not decided. The INVISIBLE HAND (Smith), price-as-information (Hayek), and the honest catalogue of MARKET FAILURES: monopoly, externalities, asymmetric information, bubbles. Two-layer: the mechanism is core economics; how far to trust markets vs regulate is the central political-economic argument. Rhymes with the biosphere's emergence corpus (order from local rules). Smith/Marshall/Hayek/Keynes cited. LIVE supply-demand interactive (drag to shift demand). Vellum (no black) + market-green + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents."),
   ("bitcoin", "BITCOIN · BTC", "#f7931a", "agora · money by cryptographic consensus · the 4th theory · interactive · vellum", "BITCOIN (BTC) — an AGORA teardown, render-not-invent: money as CONSENSUS, the fourth theory after [[money]]'s commodity / credit / state trio. A ledger no one owns that everyone can verify. ⚑ TWO REAL machines, not faked — computed live on a synchronous SHA-256 that self-tests against the standard vector before it runs: (1) a TAMPER-EVIDENT HASH CHAIN — mine blocks to a 00-prefix, then edit any block and watch its hash break and cascade red (the property Nakamoto used to drop the trusted third party); (2) a PROOF-OF-WORK MINER — pick a difficulty and find a real nonce, with a genuine live hashrate (this tab does ~70k H/s; an ASIC does ~100 trillion, which is why real difficulty targets ~19 leading zero bits not 4 hex digits — same algorithm, ~15 orders of magnitude apart). ⚑ THE HONEST SUPPLY: not 21,000,000 — the protocol counts integer satoshis and floors each halving, so the true cap is 20,999,999.9769 BTC, ~0.0231 short (verified in Python); 33 halvings, ~4 yr each, last subsidy ~2140. Two-layer: SETTLED (SHA-256, the hash-linked chain, PoW as Byzantine agreement, the emission arithmetic, double-spend solved under honest majority) vs STILL CONTESTED (is it money? energy cost? decentralization theater? value vs speculation) — flagged as a live argument, not resolved. Explicit NOT INVESTMENT ADVICE (no price, no forecast, no recommendation). Ties [[money]], [[the-market]] (bubbles), [[the-graveyard]] ($0.0386). Sources: Nakamoto 2008, the protocol rules, FIPS 180-4. Inverse: [[shintaku]]. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-ledger", "THE LEDGER · LDG", "#b8895a", "agora · Enheduanna baseline · writing was born to count grain · interactive · vellum", "THE LEDGER (LDG) — an AGORA teardown, render-not-invent, on the ENHEDUANNA BASELINE. ⚑ Writing was invented to COUNT, not to compose: the oldest unambiguous writing (Uruk IV proto-cuneiform ~3350–3200 BCE) is temple accounting — ~85% administrative (rations, receipts, inventories of grain/livestock/labour), the sign picturing the thing counted. It stayed a NAMELESS ledger for ~1,000 years: literature appears only ~2600 BCE (Fara/Abu Salabikh), and named first-person authorship — [[enheduanna]] (c.2300 BCE, entu-priestess of Nanna at Ur, daughter of Sargon) — ~1,000 yrs after the first anonymous tablets. She is the moment the tool built to count grain learned to say I — same script, same clay, same reed. ⚑ TWO live machines (real, in-browser): the BULLA BREAKER (drop commodity tokens into a sealed clay envelope, impress the surface, verify the count WITHOUT breaking the seal, then flatten the redundant tokens into a TABLET — that flattening IS the birth-of-writing step in Schmandt-Besserat thesis) with an honesty toggle that greys the contested complex-token to word-sign step; and a BASE-60 divisibility calculator (60 splits 12 ways vs 100 nine — real arithmetic, why sexagesimal was chosen). Two-layer: SETTLED (Uruk dating, tokens-in-bullae, the millennial gap, base-60 for discrete counting) vs CONTESTED (the token thesis edges — Englund/Zimansky/Damerow; ~13 metrologies not one uniform base-60; her authorship survives only in Old-Babylonian MSS ~500–600 yrs later, first named author traditional not settled). ⚠ NEVER claims she was an accountant or wrote on a ledger — the tie is the shared script and the true gap, flagged at both ends. Web-verified (CDLI, Schmandt-Besserat + critics). Inverse: [[yohaku]]. Ties [[the-shekel]], [[money]]. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-shekel", "THE SHEKEL · SHK", "#c2922e", "agora · Enheduanna baseline · money by weight, 1700 yrs before the coin · interactive · vellum", "THE SHEKEL (SHK) — an AGORA teardown, render-not-invent, ENHEDUANNA BASELINE. ⚑ The standard inflation erodes — a unit of value — is as old as Enheduanna, and it was a WEIGHT, not a coin: the shekel (Akkadian siqlu, to weigh) ~8.3 g = 180 barley-grains = 1/60 mina, a weight-denominated unit of account for silver and barley. You WEIGHED your money on a balance; you did not count it. ⚑ COINAGE is ~1,700 YEARS LATER (Lydian electrum ~610–600 BCE, then Croesus bimetallic staters ~550 BCE — web-verified). Mesopotamia ran a dual unit of account (barley by volume + silver by weight); prices/wages are on tablets, so ancient price-change is MEASURABLE. Live machine: THE BALANCE — settle a purchase by adding shekel-weights until the beam is level (verified: 2.5 shk = 1+1+half = 20.8 g = 450 grains), with a barley/silver unit-of-account toggle and a GREYED strike a coin? not for ~1,700 years (the honest negative that keeps the anchor truthful). Two-layer: SETTLED (shekel-as-weight, dual standard, tablet-prices, Lydia date) vs CONTESTED (the weight varied ~7–17 g by era, ~8.3 is THE common standard not a constant; money origin — barter/Menger vs credit/Graeber — is [[money]] debate, not re-fought here). ⚠ TWO HARD FLAGS: coined money is ~1,700 yrs after her — hers was weighed, never struck; and the surviving attestation of siqlu is c.2150 BCE under Naram-Sin, after her — the claim is about the STANDARD, not her signature. Inverse: [[muryo]]. Ties [[the-ledger]], [[money]], [[the-market]]. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("debasement", "DEBASEMENT · DBS", "#8a8f96", "agora · Enheduanna baseline · how a standard rots while its name stays · interactive · vellum", "DEBASEMENT (DBS) — an AGORA teardown, render-not-invent, ENHEDUANNA BASELINE. ⚑ A monetary standard erodes two ways that must never be collapsed: of the STANDARD (less metal for the same name — light coins, short-weight, a clipped rim) and by ALLOY (same weight, silver swapped for copper). Alloy debasement needs a struck coin passing by its face, so it is the YOUNGER form; standard-erosion is as old as the weighed shekel — which is why Enheduanna's coinless world (no coin for ~1,700 yrs) could only be cheated the first way. ⚑ THREE live machines: a two-series Roman denarius fineness BAND (surface/Walker vs bulk-core/Butcher-Ponting — the ~15-point method gap drawn as width, not hidden; near-pure under Augustus to a few-percent billon by the 260s); a DEBASE-THE-MINT toy showing Gresham's Law is CONDITIONAL — good money flees only under a mispriced legal-tender peg and reverses (Thiers) when people may discount the bad coin; and a two-attacks coin (clip the rim vs swap in copper). Two-layer: SETTLED (two forms + ordering, Nero AD64 first debasement, antoninianus fiduciary from day one, method-variance, Gresham's preconditions) vs CONTESTED (exact fineness is method-dependent; debasement to collapse is not a proven sole cause; Gresham is not universal; ancient weights were BOUNDED not runaway ~5-6pct variation; inflation at 2300 BCE is anachronistic). ⚠ Enheduanna is ERA + SCRIPT only, never a mint official; seigniorage names who gains (the antoninianus hid a 25pct cut). Web-verified (Butcher and Ponting; Rolnick and Weber; Ialongo PNAS 2021; Cripps CDLJ). Inverse: [[meberi]]. Ties [[the-shekel]], [[debt]], [[money]], [[bitcoin]]. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("debt", "DEBT · DEB", "#a5542e", "agora · Enheduanna baseline · the obligation that predates the coin · interactive · vellum", "DEBT (DEB) — an AGORA teardown, render-not-invent, ENHEDUANNA BASELINE. ⚑ Money did not begin as a coin: interest-bearing CREDIT is attested in cuneiform from the 3rd millennium BCE — temple/palace accounts, loans, interest in weighed silver and barley — roughly 1,700 yrs BEFORE the first coin. The interest had a name, mash (also 'young goat', the same offspring image as Greek tokos, Latin faenus), a rate, and, when it crushed too many, a cancellation: a royal decree of ama-gi, 'return to the mother.' ⚑ Live machine: a clay debt-tablet where mash COMPOUNDS at the standard ~20pct/yr silver (doubles in 3.8 yr) or ~33 1/3pct barley — 1 mina to 6.19 mina in ten years — and an AMA-GI clean-slate button that zeroes it, each pinned to its true date. Two-layer: SETTLED (credit before coinage, mainstream and independent of Graeber; mash + the rates as norms/legal caps in Eshnunna and Hammurabi; the amargi decrees at Lagash c.2400 BCE; misharum/andurarum edicts later; ama-gi = 'return to the mother' = release from debt-bondage) vs CONTESTED (Graeber's WHOLE myth-of-barter thesis is contested though credit-before-coins is not; 'first word for freedom' is KRAMER's hedged claim about debt-release, not political liberty; mash=goat is a metaphor not a mechanism, Hudson's 'baby fraction'; the rates are norms not one statute; Enheduanna is an era anchor only). ⚠ DATE-GAP is the headline: the famous Babylonian misharum edicts are 500-700 yrs AFTER her — the amargi contemporary with her is the Lagash one. Debt-bondage was real and harsh; the clean slate was a royal tool, not charity. Web-verified (Graeber; Hudson JESHO 2000; Kramer 1963; Code of Hammurabi). Inverse: [[oime]]. Ties [[the-ledger]], [[the-shekel]], [[debasement]], [[money]]. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("game-theory", "GAME THEORY · GAM", "#b0445a", "polemos · the math of strategy · interactive · vellum · 10", "GAME THEORY (GAM) — anchor of UD0's new 22nd domain POLEMOS (conflict & strategy). The math of the bind where your best move depends on the other player's: the PRISONER'S DILEMMA, the NASH EQUILIBRIUM, zero-sum, the payoff matrix, the tragedy of the commons. And how cooperation survives a world built to punish it — the ITERATED game, tit-for-tat (Axelrod), the shadow of the future. Cross-links the-quorum-engine + the life-science thread (cooperation among cells/ants/microbes is game theory in the wild). Two-layer: the theorems are rigorous; real people are not perfect payoff-maximizers (flagged). von Neumann (d.1957) + Nash (d.2015) MINTED in memoriam; living cited. LIVE spatial-PD interactive. Vellum (no black) + crimson + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the polemos realm beside its hub [[the-rarefaction]]."),
   ("the-art-of-war", "THE ART OF WAR · WAR", "#6a6a8a", "polemos · strategy through the ages · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE ART OF WAR (WAR) — a POLEMOS sphere: strategy as bending force to a purpose — winning, ideally, without fighting. Sun Tzu's indirect approach + deception, Clausewitz's FRICTION + the fog of war + war as the continuation of politics by other means, and the recurring geometry of advantage: flanking/envelopment, the high ground, the initiative, surprise. TROPES & UNDERCURRENTS: the wisdom is psychological as much as physical; kept honest — strategy is the rationalization of violence, studied without celebrating the cost. Render-not-invent; Sun Tzu (5th c. BCE) + Clausewitz (d.1831) MINTED in memoriam, NO copyrighted translation reproduced. LIVE envelopment interactive. Vellum (no black) + steel + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the polemos realm beside its hub [[the-rarefaction]]."),
   ("deterrence", "DETERRENCE · DET", "#4a6a9a", "polemos · the strategy of not-fighting · interactive · vellum · 10", "DETERRENCE (DET) — a POLEMOS sphere: the strangest victory, the war that never happens. Making an attack so costly no one starts it. The SECURITY DILEMMA, MUTUAL ASSURED DESTRUCTION (peace by terror), the arms race, second-strike, brinkmanship, credibility, the red line, the balance of terror. STRICTLY two-layer: the security dilemma + MAD + deterrence theory are core IR and the Cold War didn't go hot — BUT it rests on perfect rationality + zero accident over indefinite time, a bet NOT pretended safe; the near-misses are real, the equilibrium fragile (flagged, not glorified). The applied edge of game-theory + the dark twin of the art-of-war. Schelling (d.2016) MINTED. LIVE balance-of-terror interactive. Vellum (no black) + cold blue + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the polemos realm beside its hub [[the-rarefaction]]."),
   ("the-liminal", "THE LIMINAL · LIM", "#7a6aa8", "metaxy · betwixt and between · interactive · vellum · 9", "THE LIMINAL (LIM) — the human anchor of METAXÝ (the between, 15th domain). The threshold state every passage crosses through: no longer the old self, not yet the new. van Gennep's three-part rite of passage (separation -> the liminal phase -> reincorporation) + Victor Turner's BETWIXT-AND-BETWEEN and COMMUNITAS (the leveling bond of those passing through together). The immigrant, the adolescent, the society between regimes — uncomfortable because unfinished, powerful for the same reason. Metaxu (Plato's Diotima / Simone Weil): the between that both separates AND connects. Two-layer: the anthropology is foundational; 'liminal' as buzzword flagged as metaphor. van Gennep/Turner/Weil minted in memoriam; living cited. LIVE rite-of-passage interactive. Vellum (no black) + twilight-violet + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents. &middot; homed in the metaxy realm beside its hub [[langtons-loop]]."),
   ("the-edge-of-chaos", "THE EDGE OF CHAOS · EOC", "#b0663a", "metaxy · between order and chaos · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE EDGE OF CHAOS (EOC) — the scientific heart of METAXÝ. The thin critical regime between frozen ORDER and pure CHAOS, where structure is stable enough to persist and fluid enough to change — and where computation, life, and maybe mind prefer to live. Langton's lambda (the dial), Rule 110 (proven universal computation, sitting right at the edge), Wolfram's Class IV, and Per Bak's SELF-ORGANIZED CRITICALITY (the sandpile that tunes itself to the critical slope; avalanches of every size — earthquakes, extinctions, neuronal cascades). The direct BRIDGE to the life-science CA spheres + quantum-cellular-automata. ⚠ two-layer: the taxonomy + Rule 110 + SOC are rigorous, but 'life/cognition operate at the edge' is an influential HYPOTHESIS, not settled law (flagged). Langton/Kauffman/Wolfram living cited; Bak (d.2002) minted. LIVE elementary-CA regime sweep (order/edge/chaos). Vellum (no black) + ember + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the metaxy realm beside its hub [[langtons-loop]]."),
   ("the-interface", "THE INTERFACE · IFC", "#2f8a8a", "metaxy · the surface where two meet · interactive · vellum · 9", "THE INTERFACE (IFC) — METAXÝ as surface: the boundary that both separates and connects (Simone Weil's metaxu — the wall two prisoners tap through). The thinnest, most important part of any system, where inside meets outside without becoming one: the cell MEMBRANE, the skin, the software interface/API, the channel between two minds. Selective permeability (the chooser, not the wall), the protocol (the agreed grammar), the threshold of perception (world->mind). Catalysis on surfaces, meaning in the narrow band — the between is not empty space, it is where everything happens. ⚠ two-layer: each case (membrane/skin/surface/API) is real and concrete; treating them as ONE idea is a unifying METAPHOR offered as analogy, not a claim that biology and software share laws (labeled). Weil (d.1943) minted. LIVE permeable-membrane interactive (toggle the pores). Vellum (no black) + teal + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents. &middot; homed in the metaxy realm beside its hub [[langtons-loop]]."),
   ("the-cyborg", "THE CYBORG · CYB", "#6a6ab8", "metaxy · between organism and machine · interactive · vellum · 9", "THE CYBORG (CYB) — METAXÝ at the human/machine seam: the hybrid that belongs to neither side. Donna Haraway's cyborg (the being of the between, refusing the clean splits) + the ordinary reality already here: PACEMAKERS, cochlear implants, nerve-reading prosthetics, brain-computer interfaces, the extended mind (memory in the device). To merge with a tool is to gain its powers AND inherit its vulnerabilities — extended and exposed in the same motion. Bridges the AI domain (machine half) + life-science (organism half); cousin to organoid-intelligence. ⚠ STRICTLY two-layer: pacemakers/implants/prosthetics/BCIs are real working medicine helping millions; 'merging with AI' / mind-uploading / full neural integration are speculative or early-stage (separated from the deployed tech); Haraway treated as a philosophical LENS, not a forecast. Haraway LIVING -> cited not minted. LIVE neuron<->circuit morph interactive. Vellum (no black) + steel-violet + quorum-ring favicon. 9 emergents. &middot; homed in the metaxy realm beside its hub [[langtons-loop]]."),
   ("the-chain-of-thought", "THE CHAIN OF THOUGHT · COT", "#6a4fc0", "niphelektron · pipeline 5 · reasoning as iterated prediction · interactive · vellum · 10", "THE CHAIN OF THOUGHT (COT) — the CAPSTONE of the NIPHELEKTRON inference pipeline (tokenize -> embed -> transform -> predict -> REASON, looped). The 2024-2025 frontier: predict not one token but a long chain of working-out, spend more compute at inference, and a model's answers on hard problems jump. Chain-of-thought prompting (Wei 2022), self-consistency, test-time / inference-time SCALING (a second scaling axis beyond model size), the verifier, adaptive effort. The reasoning-model wave -- OpenAI o1/o3, DeepSeek-R1, Google thinking models, Claude's extended/adaptive thinking -- cited as public fact, not minted. Cross-links the-quorum-engine + the AI domain. STRICTLY two-layer: the gains are real and measured, BUT it is still next-token prediction (not a proof engine), more thinking is not always better, and FAITHFULNESS is an open problem -- a stated chain of thought is not guaranteed to be the true cause of the answer (flagged, load-bearing). LIVE bat-and-ball demo: answer-directly (fast, wrong) vs think-it-through (a streamed scratchpad, right) with a token counter. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 10 emergents. &middot; homed in the niphelektron realm beside its hub [[the-top-p]]."),
   ("the-temperature", "THE TEMPERATURE &middot; how wild the electron wanders", "#7488e6", "niphelektron &middot; softmax temperature + sampling; 2D odds / 3D blizzard / expanded toddler snow-game &middot; lit+amber", "THE TEMPERATURE &mdash; on THE ELECTRON's bench (the inference layer). Temperature is the one dial deciding how wild the next-token wander is: cold spikes the odds to one word (a straight, safe line), hot flattens the blizzard until every word is nearly equal (chaos). Built on the three-corner layout (2D odds / 3D blizzard / EXPANDED toddler snow-GAME): slide T, watch the bars reshape and the storm thicken, then TAP THE STORM to send the electron tumbling onto a word. &#9670; LIT: real p_i = softmax(logit_i / T), recomputed live; the ENTROPY in bits is exact (max = log&#8322;10 &asymp; 3.32), and the toddler's landing TALLY converges to the true odds (TOP's fairness check &mdash; tap enough, frequency &rarr; probability). &#9650; AMBER: ten toy logits for one prompt stand in for a real ~50k vocabulary; no model runs. Kept by THE ELECTRON, TOP's check. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-top-p", "THE NUCLEUS &middot; top-p sampling", "#7488e6", "niphelektron &middot; nucleus (top-p) sampling; keep the head, cut the tail; 2D/3D/toddler &middot; lit+amber", "THE NUCLEUS (top-p) &mdash; on THE ELECTRON's bench. You needn't let the electron wander the whole blizzard: nucleus sampling keeps only the smallest set of top words whose odds together reach p &mdash; the nucleus &mdash; and discards the long tail entirely, so it can be adventurous without ever landing on nonsense. Slide the cutoff on the three-corner layout; TAP THE STORM and the electron only ever lands inside the kept set (the tail never lights up). &#9670; LIT: the exact top-p algorithm (Holtzman et al., 2019) &mdash; sort, accumulate to p, renormalise, sample; the kept-set size, the cut tail and the true coverage recompute live. &#9650; AMBER: ten toy logits at fixed T=0.9 stand in for a real vocabulary; no model runs. Sibling to [[the-temperature]]. Kept by THE ELECTRON. David Lee Wise / ROOT0, with AVAN."),
   ("the-nes", "THE NES · NES", "#3a7a9a", "exereunesis · 8-bit teardown + spec edition · interactive · vellum · 12", "THE NES (NES) — the first sphere of UD0's new 23rd domain EXEREÚNESIS (ἐξερεύνησις, the searching-out): TECHNICAL TEARDOWNS. A full 8-bit Nintendo (1985) hardware teardown + SPEC EDITION. Almost nothing inside: two custom Ricoh chips, 2 KB RAM, a slot. The 2A03 (MOS 6502 core @ 1.79 MHz + the APU on-die), the 2C02 PPU (256x240, 64 sprites / 8 per scanline = the flicker, 54-color palette ~25 on screen), the 5-channel APU, the 2 KB work RAM, and the CARTRIDGE + MAPPER (MMC1/MMC3 bank-switching that kept upgrading the machine for a decade). Plus the 10NES lockout chip + the wear-prone 72-pin connector (the real roots of the blinking power light), the serial controller, NTSC composite out. ⚠ two-layer: chips/clocks/memory-map/sprite limits are documented FACT; the blinking-light + lockout-arms-race LORE is flagged (well-supported version, not the tall tale). Render-not-invent; NO ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; Nintendo/Ricoh + NESdev cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip -> its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + blueprint-slate + quorum-ring favicon. 12 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("sega-master-system", "SEGA MASTER SYSTEM · SMS", "#b0443a", "exereunesis · 8-bit teardown · 1985/86", "SEGA MASTER SYSTEM (SMS) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Sega's answer to the NES: a sharper 8-bit machine built around the Zilog Z80, with more colours and a video chip descended from the Texas Instruments line. It outsold the NES in Europe and Brazil even as it lost the US, and its silicon carried straight over into the Game Gear handheld. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("snes", "SUPER NINTENDO · SNES · SNS", "#6a5aa0", "exereunesis · 16-bit teardown · 1990", "SUPER NINTENDO · SNES (SNS) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Nintendo's 16-bit machine paired a 65C816 CPU with two custom picture units and a Sony-designed sound system, and famously left room in the cartridge for extra chips. Mode 7's rotating, scaling backgrounds and add-on silicon like the Super FX kept it competitive for years. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-genesis", "SEGA GENESIS · MEGA DRIVE", "#2f6a9a", "exereunesis · 16-bit teardown · 1988/89", "SEGA GENESIS · MEGA DRIVE (GEN) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Sega's 16-bit contender ran on a Motorola 68000 — the same CPU class as the era's workstations and arcade boards — with a Z80 kept on board to run sound and stay compatible with the Master System. Its FM synthesis gave it a punchy, distinctive voice and the 'blast processing' swagger. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("turbografx-16", "TURBOGRAFX-16 · PC ENGINE · TG6", "#b0703a", "exereunesis · teardown · 1987", "TURBOGRAFX-16 · PC ENGINE (TG6) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. NEC and Hudson's tiny machine punched far above its size: an 8-bit CPU core paired with a 16-bit video chip, a huge sprite budget, and a credit-card game format. It was first to market with a CD-ROM add-on, opening the door to the multimedia generation. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-playstation", "SONY PLAYSTATION · PS1 · PSX", "#6a6a8a", "exereunesis · 32-bit teardown · 1994", "SONY PLAYSTATION · PS1 (PSX) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Sony's first console put a 32-bit MIPS CPU, a dedicated geometry coprocessor, and a CD-ROM drive into one cheap box — and made real-time 3-D the default. Affordable polygons and cheap discs broke the cartridge era open and turned Sony into the industry leader overnight. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-saturn", "SEGA SATURN", "#5a7a9a", "exereunesis · 32-bit teardown · 1994", "SEGA SATURN (SAT) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Sega's powerful, notoriously complex 32-bit machine packed two main CPUs, two video processors, and a clutch of helper chips — eight processors in all. Brilliant at 2-D and capable in 3-D, it was also famously hard to program, which blunted its fight against the PlayStation. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-n64", "NINTENDO 64 · N64", "#2f8a6a", "exereunesis · 64-bit teardown · 1996", "NINTENDO 64 (N64) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Nintendo's 64-bit machine teamed a MIPS CPU with a Silicon Graphics coprocessor that did both graphics and sound, and stuck with cartridges for speed and security. It pioneered the analog stick and rumble, and made smooth 3-D worlds — at the cost of blurry textures and tiny cartridge storage. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-dreamcast", "SEGA DREAMCAST · DC", "#3a8aa0", "exereunesis · 128-bit-era teardown · 1998", "SEGA DREAMCAST (DC) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Sega's final console arrived early and forward-looking: a fast Hitachi SH-4 CPU, a PowerVR graphics chip, a built-in modem for online play, and a memory card with its own screen. Brilliant and beloved, it was undone by the PS2's hype and Sega's finances. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-ps2", "SONY PLAYSTATION 2 · PS2", "#3a4a8a", "exereunesis · 128-bit teardown · 2000", "SONY PLAYSTATION 2 · PS2 (PS2) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. The best-selling console ever built its case on two things: a wildly powerful, eccentric custom CPU called the Emotion Engine, and a DVD drive that also made it the cheapest DVD player in the house. Hard to program, backward-compatible with the PS1, and unstoppable in the market. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-gamecube", "NINTENDO GAMECUBE · GCN", "#6a5aa8", "exereunesis · teardown · 2001", "NINTENDO GAMECUBE (GCN) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Nintendo's compact purple cube was an efficient, developer-friendly machine: an IBM PowerPC 'Gekko' CPU, an ATI 'Flipper' GPU with fast embedded memory, and tiny proprietary mini-discs. Underrated power in an unusually clean architecture — held back mainly by its small media and lack of DVD playback. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-xbox", "MICROSOFT XBOX · XBX", "#4a8a5a", "exereunesis · teardown · 2001", "MICROSOFT XBOX (XBX) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Microsoft's first console was essentially a custom PC: an Intel Pentium III, an NVIDIA GPU, a hard drive, and Ethernet built in. That PC heritage made it powerful and easy to develop for, and the built-in HDD plus Xbox Live laid the groundwork for modern online console gaming. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-xbox-360", "XBOX 360 · X36", "#4a9a5a", "exereunesis · teardown · 2005", "XBOX 360 (X36) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Microsoft's second console led the HD generation with a triple-core PowerPC CPU and an ATI GPU that pioneered unified shaders. Fast, online-first, and developer-friendly, it was nearly derailed by the 'Red Ring of Death' — one of the most infamous hardware-reliability failures in console history. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-ps3", "SONY PLAYSTATION 3 · PS3", "#4a5a8a", "exereunesis · teardown · 2006", "SONY PLAYSTATION 3 · PS3 (PS3) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. The PS3's heart was the Cell Broadband Engine — a radical processor with one general core and seven specialised math engines — paired with an NVIDIA GPU and, crucially, a Blu-ray drive. Brilliant and bafflingly hard to program, expensive at launch, it nonetheless won the format war for Blu-ray. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-wii", "NINTENDO WII", "#3a9aa8", "exereunesis · teardown · 2006", "NINTENDO WII (WII) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. Nintendo skipped the HD arms race and won the generation on a different axis: motion control. Modest, efficient PowerPC silicon — essentially an overclocked GameCube — drove a runaway hit because the magic was in the Wii Remote's sensors, not the teraflops. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
   ("the-ps4", "SONY PLAYSTATION 4 · PS4", "#2f5a9a", "exereunesis · teardown · 2013", "SONY PLAYSTATION 4 · PS4 (PS4) — a UD0 EXEREÚNESIS console TEARDOWN + spec edition. After the PS3's exotic difficulty, Sony went straight for ease: a single AMD chip combining eight x86 cores and a Radeon GPU, with a large pool of fast GDDR5 shared between them. Developer-friendly, well-priced, and clearly led its generation. Render-not-invent, two-layer (datasheet fact vs marketing/lore); no ROMs/BIOS/code reproduced; manufacturer cited not minted. LIVE clickable block-diagram teardown (click a chip → its spec) + a spec sheet. Vellum (no black) + quorum-ring favicon. 7 components. &middot; homed in the exereunesis realm beside its hub [[tera]]."),
