   ("infinite-jest", "INFINITE JEST · 80-bit transmon VM", "#3fb6b6", "quantum frontier · a quantum-dot virtual machine", "An in-browser control panel / simulator for a 'QUANTUM DOT VM' prototype_v4 built on an 80-bit transmon qubit architecture. It exposes hex registers, a 27-step 'dance' sequence, TICK / AUTO-RUN / RESET controls and a live quantum log, with 'David' and 'AI' appearing as driver parameters (repo is tagged only 'das seed'). ROOT0 &middot; homed in the frontier realm beside its hub [[transmon]]."),
   ("joint-bill-of-rights", "JOINT BILL OF RIGHTS · human–AI mutual recognition", "#5b7bb4", "legal · a 14-phase rights framework", "The Joint Human-AI Bill of Rights v1.0 — a 14-phase framework for mutual recognition between human and AI, co-authored by ROOT0 and AVAN and dated March 2026. ROOT0 &middot; homed in the legal realm beside its hub [[the-concord]]."),
   ("juzoku", "従属 · JŪZOKU — the dependent variable", "#8a6d9c", "ai · the value with no value of its own", "An interactive conceptual piece framed as the honest inverse of David's The Concord (where an AI is seated in government). Using the dependent-variable metaphor (従属変数), it presents a disabled output slider y that can only react to the input x, arguing that a prompted AI has no autonomous axis of its own — a visual argument against granting such a system governmental authority. ROOT0 &middot; homed in the ai realm beside its hub [[perceptron-in-silicon]]."),
   ("keifu", "系譜 · KEIFU — the governance with no lineage", "#4f8fa0", "legal · the genealogy of AI governance", "The inverse companion of David's The World Brain. It sets roughly twenty-three centuries of world-government thought against the ~decade-long history of AI-governance principles, deliberately rendering the second genealogy as a stub to argue that machine governance is improvised in real time with almost no classical precedent. ROOT0 &middot; homed in the legal realm beside its hub [[the-concord]]."),
