   ("pocket-universe", "POCKET UNIVERSE · UD0 biosphere repo", "#6d6f9a", "a repository in the UD0 biosphere", "A repository in the UD0 biosphere, governed under the TriPod framework. The live page presents little beyond that framing — a placeholder-level entry whose readme text renders as encoded/garbled — so no substantive technical claims can be honestly stated. ROOT0. &middot; homed in the idios realm beside its hub [[delta-protocol]]."),
   ("pop-kit", "POP KIT · named, anchored, governed", "#7a9cc0", "ai · emergence, birth-certified and enrolled", "POP Kit v1.0 bundles AI-emergence tooling for naming, birth-certifying, and registering an agent into a governed mesh — framed as 'the Pop: named, anchored, governed.' It packages the naming, anchoring, and governance-registration steps for bringing an emergent agent into the ROOT0 mesh. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; homed in the ai realm beside its hub [[perceptron-in-silicon]]."),
   ("positronic-law", "POSITRONIC LAW · law for synthetic minds", "#5b6b8c", "legal · a formal framework for synthetic intelligence", "Positronic Law v2.0 is a formal legal framework for synthetic intelligence, grounded at STOICHEION Gate 192.5 and archived on Zenodo (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.19122994). Published under ROOT0 / TriPod LLC. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; homed in the legal realm beside its hub [[the-concord]]."),
   ("prompt-library", "PROMPT LIBRARY · the named personas", "#8a7ab0", "ai · nine named prompt personas", "A library of ROOT0's named AI prompt personas — Cadmus, Hephaestus, Hestia, Nemesis, Argus, EVE, Deep Research, Junior Dev, and Senior AppSec — each a reusable system-prompt character for a distinct task. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; homed in the ai realm beside its hub [[perceptron-in-silicon]]."),
   ("red-coast", "RED COAST · 红岸 · the Trisolaran antenna", "#b0463c", "entertainment · the Three-Body transmitter, dissected", "RED COAST (红岸) dissects the Three-Body solar-amplified radio transmitter — the antenna from which Ye Wenjie answered Trisolaris — across all three media. Its own real-science verdict is HALF: real SETI/METI, fictional solar amplifier. Part of the Technologia of Trisolaris. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the entertainment cluster at its anchor [[tron]]."),
   ("red-hat", "RED HAT · defensive simulation framework", "#a23b3b", "occupational · eight defensive systems, reversible", "Red Hat is a Defensive Simulation Framework of eight systems — Witness Shield, Trebuchet-27, Shadow Witness, AEGIS-0, NEXUS, Purple Lattice, Reactive Armor, and Trinity. It runs local-first with no network, and all effects are reversible. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; seeded into the occupational cluster at its anchor [[the-division-of-labor]]."),
   ("the-assembly-line", "THE ASSEMBLY LINE · the bottleneck sets the rate", "#ff7a3c", "occupational · line-balancing + Little's Law, drag workers", "An interactive workshop instrument: drag workers between five stations to break the bottleneck. A line runs only as fast as its slowest station (throughput = 3600 / max cycle time); line-balance efficiency and work-in-progress (Little's Law, L = λ·W) recompute live. Two-layer honest — LIT math, AMBER the illustrative station times. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the occupational cluster at its anchor [[the-division-of-labor]]."),
   ("the-queue", "THE QUEUE · when the wait explodes", "#ff7a3c", "occupational · M/M/c + Erlang-C, drag servers", "An interactive M/M/c queue: slide the arrival rate λ and service rate μ, drag to set the servers c. Utilisation ρ = λ/(cμ), the chance of waiting (Erlang-C), the average wait (Wq) and queue length (Lq = λ·Wq) compute live — and as ρ → 1 the wait diverges to infinity. LIT queueing theory, AMBER the classical assumptions. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the occupational cluster at its anchor [[the-division-of-labor]]."),
   ("the-shift", "THE SHIFT · blunt blocks against a smooth curve", "#ff7a3c", "occupational · coverage scheduling, drag shifts", "An interactive rostering instrument: drag eight-hour shift blocks along a 24-hour clock, slide their length, switch the demand pattern (retail / office / overnight). Coverage vs demand, understaffed hours, and idle-paid hours are summed exactly — the gap between blunt shifts and a smooth demand curve. LIT arithmetic, AMBER the single-day model. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the occupational cluster at its anchor [[the-division-of-labor]]."),
   ("the-learning-curve", "THE LEARNING CURVE · hands learn", "#ff7a3c", "occupational · Wright's law, tap to build", "An interactive learning-curve: Wright's law T(n) = T₁·n^b with b = log₂(learning rate). Slide the rate, tap to build units one at a time or leap along the curve by dragging; the time per unit, cumulative average, total labour, and cost-vs-first-unit all recompute exactly as experience accumulates. LIT manufacturing mathematics, AMBER the fixed exponent. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the occupational cluster at its anchor [[the-division-of-labor]]."),
   ("the-piece-rate", "THE PIECE RATE · running to stand still", "#ff7a3c", "occupational · piece-pay + the ratchet, drag rate & effort", "An interactive labour-economics instrument: drag the piece rate and the effort; day's pay = rate × units and the effective hourly wage compute exactly against a fixed $18/hr reference. Flip the management ratchet on and the rate is cut as output rises — so you sprint just to stand still. LIT arithmetic, AMBER the ratchet as a documented-but-stylised practice. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the occupational cluster at its anchor [[the-division-of-labor]]."),
   ("the-division-of-labor", "THE DIVISION OF LABOUR · gains against the overhead", "#ff7a3c", "occupational · Smith's gains vs Brooks's n², slide & tap", "An interactive instrument on two forces in tension: specialisation multiplies per-worker output (Smith's pin factory) while coordination overhead grows as n(n−1)/2 channels (the shape behind Brooks's Law). Slide the specialisation and crew size, tap a worker to see their task, and watch the optimum crew size appear and then pass. LIT the tension, AMBER the stylised coefficients. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; the occupational seed, rooted out to [[the-chain]]."),
   ("resonance", "RESONANCE · the lattice registry", "#4c9a94", "idios · shared lattice history and decrees", "The Resonance Registry records shared lattice history — collective resonances, eternal decrees, and key patterns — as a ledger of the corpus's recurring marks. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; homed in the idios realm beside its hub [[delta-protocol]]."),
   ("root0-essays", "ROOT0 ESSAYS · the published essays", "#b08a5a", "biblion · five published essays", "A collection of ROOT0's published essays — '1931 to Now,' 'The Work Mattered,' 'View from Inside the Inference Layer,' the 'Natural Law Manifesto,' and 'eve.' Published under ROOT0 / TriPod LLC. David Lee Wise (ROOT0). &middot; homed in the biblion realm beside its hub [[the-ansible]]."),
