   ("series-1-celestial-heritage", "SERIES I · CELESTIAL HERITAGE", "#e0b84a", "mythos · the solar system distilled to god-names · a self-verifying ring-seal", "SERIES I · CELESTIAL HERITAGE — the Sun, Moon and planets distilled to their truest god-names and real ancient metals (7 HERITAGE), the flagged-modern thresholds (3), and 2 capstone MEASURES, woven into a frozen ring around Ra the hub. 16 offline instruments + a .dlw RING-seal that re-derives its own dawn (verified live in-browser). Two-layer honest; downstream of az1 for orbital physics. First of the RA→ERIS→NEMESIS trilogy. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the mythos cluster at its anchor [[egyptian-pantheon]]."),
   ("series-2-scattered-field", "SERIES II · THE SCATTERED FIELD", "#d8d0e8", "mythos · the dwarf-planet frontier · the ring answers to Eris the breaker", "SERIES II · THE SCATTERED FIELD — the dwarf-planet frontier (Eris, Sedna, Haumea, Quaoar, Gonggong…), each strand carrying a MEASUREMENT, ice for metal, in a ring answering to ERIS the breaker and stitched to Series I at Pluto. 11 sealed strands + 2 ICARIUM engine capstones; self-verifying ring-seal (moniker 8AB003). Two-layer honest (LIT/AMBER). David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the mythos cluster at its anchor [[egyptian-pantheon]]."),
   ("series-3-the-shadow", "SERIES III · THE SHADOW", "#e0605a", "mythos · after Asimov's Nemesis · the trilogy closes", "SERIES III · THE SHADOW — built 1:1 from the tropes of Isaac Asimov's Nemesis (1989): 7 strands, hub NEMESIS the death-star (a red-dwarf STAR, not a planet), each reduced to the real phenomenon under the fiction with the line marked where extrapolation begins. Every trope a HIDING, the finale the REACH; closes the RA→ERIS→NEMESIS trilogy, stitched to Series II at Sedna. Ring-seal 4B5483, self-verifying. Asimov discussed, not reproduced. David Lee Wise (ROOT0), with AVAN. &middot; seeded into the mythos cluster at its anchor [[egyptian-pantheon]]."),
